	title ' Memory Manager'********************************************************************************** Memory manager  Tool Set #2** (C) Copyright 1985-1989,1991* Apple Computer, Inc.* All Rights Reserved** Original Code * by Rich Williams January 1986**       'Memory [management] is the treasury and guardian of all things'*        Cicero, De	Oratore. Bk. i, sec. 5*** RamDisk         Tool Set #13*       The ramdisk	tool has been integrated into the memory manager*       but it is a	separate tool with a separate dispatch table*** Revision 2.00** September 1986 by	Rich Williams** The patches from 1.1 have been included into the rom including:** 1) The restart routine now doesn't throw out valid handles** 2) New handles are created with ID number $F0FF** 3) The purge routines are now in the rom** Changes not part of 1.1** 1) BlockMove ignores high byte of 4 byte address** 2) Ramdisk now returns bytes transferred count on DIB call** 3) Purge and Compact optimized for banks 0 and 1. Purge in 1.1 was updated** 4) SetHandleSize makes handle temporarily unpurgable** 5) With a last minute phone patch by Steve, Fern and Mike	dictated*    by Rich at 5:52 pm on 2 Mar 87.*** Revision 3.00** Converted to MAX.** Incorporated patch?*** 25 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Made the peeker a separate entity again.  Also separated out the * equates.** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Added global variables LastLowHandle and LastHighHandle.  These are* set by SearchUp and SearchDown every time a handle is found.  Search* now calls SearchUpFast and SearchDownFast which start their searches* using the values in LastLowhandle and LastHighHandle.** DisposeHandle, DisposeAll and DoPurge all call CheckRecent to make sure* that the values in SearchUpFast and SearchDownFast are all valid.** Added debugging code to DisposeHandle and NewHandle, so that the handles* being acted on are written to a specific location.** Added conditional compile code that ignores most of BootInit when making* a version to run in RAM.  The RAM version patches the vectors and* always zeros the power byte.  It assumes all other memory manager data* structures are intact and valid.** 04 Oct 88	Steven Glass** The Original design of the OOM Queue let it run only after the memory * manager failed to make room.** By calling the Queue before the MM compacts, and purges, we can allow * for an application to write its own (and more sophisticated) purge routines.** 06 Oct 88	Steven Glass** SetHandleSize can move a handle from the used list to the purgelist if the * new size is zero.  When this happens, we have to check the recently allocated* handle so we won't start our search from the purge list.** 15 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Rewrote SearchFail code to be more understandable.  The number of * retries is now different than when rich first wrote it.  This made it * necessary to rewrite a little of the purge code to keep things working.** 23 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Changed the searchup, searchdown and fastsearchup and fastsearchdown routines* so that they would not remember the handle found if the handle was fixed bank* or fixed loc.** Added second entry point to MakeIDMask so that it would not check for non-zero* major ID.** Changed purgeall to use new entry to MakeIDMask.  Makes it possible to* purge all purgables at once.** Changed SearchFail to use new PurgeAll.** 30 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Added ClearRecent, a routine to zero the last found handles.  ClearRecent* is called at MMReset, MMBootinit and WarmStart.** 31 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Made PurgeAll return bizzare errors again.** 23 Nov 88	John Arkley** Fixed bug in RD ExecPCCmd routine to return properly when an out-of-range cmd* call is made from SmartPort due to the 'additional' SmartPort commands.** Made RAM Disk use one and only one handle.** 30 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Fixed a bug in CheckRecent where bad values were used if the handle being* passed was not valid.** Made a number of routines "public" for use with the patch file.** Changed DisposeAll to check the calling routine to make sure that * the caller is not disposing of himself.  This mistake seems to be * common in appications and somehow they were lucky until recently.** 21 Dec 88	Steven Glass** Incorporated SetHandleSize patch so that handle is re-derefed after resized* in case it moves.** 08 Jan 89	Steven Glass** Also zeroed the FirstOOMPtr in BootInit and Reset so that OOM queue is cleared.** 19 Jan 89	John Arkley** Fix RAMDISK routine MAKEDISK to clear stack before error exit so it RTSs back* back to the initcommand routine with an error.** 16 Feb 89	Harry Yee** Calls DeleteFromOOMQueue and AddToOOMQueue were not passing error codes to* the exit routines. BRC #41432, 41841.** 3/31/89	Mensch** Fixed OOMQueue so that it would properly compare the amount of memory freed to* the amount needed.** 4/21/89	Mensch** Made disposeall not return an error when an app tries to dispose of itself.* (The dispose does not occur however...)** 11/13/89	Mensch** Fixed the verify routine so that its test for a valid handle is a little more* robust than it was before. This is for the DisposeHandle bug (DisposeHandle($fbfbfb)* would screw up the hint something horrible...) BRC#53386** 21-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Added new call $3002 SetHandleID(newID,handle):oldID.* If you pass 0 for the new ID, it just returns the old one.** 12-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Added check in DisposeHandle to disallow disposing the first handle.* This would be very bad.  Now returns error $0206.** 14-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Removed one instruction in CheckRecent to allow for the case that* LastLowHandle and LastHighHandle are equal, and are the handle that* we're disposing/etc.  In this case we need to bump *both* hints,* but it was only bumping the low one.** In case anybody does another ROM, added ClearRecent to DisposeAll* and PurgeAll (this was done long ago for the ROM 1 patch).** 19-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed XSearchFail to correctly return CLC when we run out of retry* methods.** It was accidentally returning SEC ("okay to try again"), and this* was causing a long hang and then a crash--we would try retry methods* number 8 through $FFFF, and then crash when we wrapped back to zero.* (This happened only if an OOMQ routine claimed to have freed up enough* memory on the *second* pass.)*********************************************************************************	string asis	eject	include 'm16.util2'	include 'm16.misctool'	include 'm16.memory'	include 'mm.macros'	include 'mm.equates.asm'	title ' Forward Address and Entries';-----------------------------------------------;;   Forward addresses and entries;;-----------------------------------------------	ENTRY BlockMove	ENTRY CheckHandle	ENTRY CompactMem	ENTRY DIB	ENTRY DisposAll	ENTRY DisposHandle	ENTRY DoPurge	ENTRY ExecPCCmd	ENTRY FindHandle	ENTRY FreeMem	ENTRY GetAttr	ENTRY GetBlockA	ENTRY GetDiskSize	ENTRY GetHandleSize	ENTRY GetNext	ENTRY GetPrev	ENTRY GetNextFree	ENTRY GetPrevFree	ENTRY HLock	ENTRY HLockAll	ENTRY HUnlock	ENTRY HUnlockAll	ENTRY HandToHand	ENTRY HandToPtr	ENTRY InsertFrBlock	ENTRY InsertFree	ENTRY InsertHandle	ENTRY InsertPurge	ENTRY Link2	ENTRY MMBootInit	ENTRY MMReset	ENTRY MMShutdown	ENTRY MMStartup	ENTRY MMStatus	ENTRY MMVersion	ENTRY MakeIDMask	ENTRY MakeIDMask2	ENTRY MaxBlock	ENTRY MoveAttr	ENTRY NewHandle	ENTRY PCControl	ENTRY PCData	ENTRY PCInit	ENTRY PCReadBlk	ENTRY PCStatus	ENTRY PCWriteBlk	ENTRY PtrToHand	ENTRY PurgeAll	ENTRY PurgeHandle	ENTRY RDLink	ENTRY ReallocHandle	ENTRY RemoveHandle	ENTRY RestoreHandle	ENTRY ScanHandles	ENTRY SearchHandle	ENTRY SearchDown	ENTRY SearchDownFast	ENTRY SearchID	ENTRY SearchUp	ENTRY SetHandleSize	ENTRY SetPurge	ENTRY SetPurgeAll	ENTRY Start0	ENTRY StartX	ENTRY StartXTop	ENTRY TestMem	ENTRY TotalMem	ENTRY TrimFree	ENTRY Validate	ENTRY VerifyH2	ENTRY VerifyHandle	ENTRY XCheckFit	ENTRY XCleanUp	ENTRY XCompact	ENTRY XCreateHandles	ENTRY XGetFree	ENTRY XLink	ENTRY XMMPatcher	ENTRY XMoveData	ENTRY XPurge	ENTRY XRealloc	ENTRY XRestart	ENTRY XSearch	ENTRY XSearchFail	ENTRY XUserPurge	ENTRY XWarmStart	ENTRY CheckRecent	ENTRY ClearRecent	ENTRY AddToOOMQueue	ENTRY DeleteFromOOMQueue	ENTRY RealFreeMem	entry SetHandleID	Title 'Call Table'********************************************************************************** Memory manager call table*  This is the dispatch table for the MM calls**  Beware!!! if it moves from $FF0000, make sure tool locator is updated*********************************************************************************	EXPORT MMCallTableMMCallTable	PROC	longa on	longi on	DC.L (TableEnd-mmCallTable)/4 ; # entries + 1	DC.L MMBootInit-1	;01 Boot time call	DC.L MMStartup-1	;02 Application init call	DC.L MMShutdown-1	;03 App quit	DC.L MMVersion-1	;04 Version #	DC.L MMReset-1	;05 Reset call	DC.L MMStatus-1	;06 Active status	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NewHandle-1	;09 NewHandle	DC.L ReallocHandle-1 ;0A ReallocHandle	DC.L RestoreHandle-1 ;0B RestoreHandle	DC.L AddToOOMQueue-1 ;0C	DC.L DeleteFromOOMQueue-1 ;0D	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L DisposHandle-1	;10 DisposHandle	DC.L DisposAll-1	;11 DisposAll	DC.L PurgeHandle-1	;12 PurgeHandle	DC.L PurgeAll-1	;13 PurgeAll	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L GetHandleSize-1 ;18 GetHandleSize	DC.L SetHandleSize-1 ;19 SetHandleSize	DC.L FindHandle-1	;1A FindHandle	DC.L FreeMem-1	;1B FreeMem	DC.L MaxBlock-1	;1C MaxBlock	DC.L TotalMem-1	;1D TotalMem	DC.L CheckHandle-1	;1E CheckHandle	DC.L CompactMem-1	;1F CompactMem	DC.L HLock-1	;20 HLock	DC.L HLockAll-1	;21 HLockAll	DC.L HUnlock-1	;22 HUnlock	DC.L HUnlockAll-1	;23 HUnlockAll	DC.L SetPurge-1	;24 SetPurge	DC.L SetPurgeAll-1	;25 SetPurgeAll	DC.L NotImp-1	;26 DeRef	DC.L NotImp-1	DC.L PtrToHand-1	;28 PtrToHand	DC.L HandToPtr-1	;29 HandToPtr	DC.L HandToHand-1	;2A HandToHand	DC.L BlockMove-1	;2B BlockMove	DC.L NotImp-1	;2C	DC.L NotImp-1	;2D	DC.L NotImp-1	;2E	DC.L RealFreeMem-1	;2F RealFreeMem	dc.l SetHandleID-1	;30 SetHandleID 21-Jan-91 DALTableEnd	eject********************************************************************************** Ram Disk call table** Beware!!! if this	moves from $FF00C0 make sure tool locator is updated*********************************************************************************	EXPORT RDCallTableRDCallTable		;       	DC.L (RDTblEnd-RDCallTable)/4 ; # entries + 1	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;01 Boot time call	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;02 Application init call	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;03 App quit	DC.L MMVersion-1	;04 Version #	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;05 Reset call	DC.L MMStatus-1	;06 Active status	DC.L RDNotImp-1	DC.L RDNotImp-1	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;09 Kill	DC.L ExecPCCmd-1	;0A Exec P.C. call	DC.L RDNotImp-1	;0B SetDiskSize	DC.L GetDiskSize-1	;0C GetDiskSize	DC.L RDNotImp-1	DC.L RDNotImp-1	DC.L RDNotImp-1RDTblEnd		; RDNotImp	jsl RDLink	jmp XCleanUpNotImp	jsl Link	;Link & Unlink to fix stack	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** ParmCnt** This table has the number of bytes of	parameters for each	call*********************************************************************************ParmCnt	PROC	DC.B 00	;01 Boot time call	DC.B 00	;02 Application init call	DC.B 02	;03 App quit	DC.B 00	;04 Version #	DC.B 00	;05 Reset	DC.B 00	;06 Status	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 12	;09 New Handle	DC.B 16	;0A ReallocHandle	DC.B 04	;0B RestoreHandle	DC.B 04	;0C AddToOOMQueue	DC.B 04	;0D DeleteFromOOMQueue	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 04	;10 DisposHandle	DC.B 02	;11 DisposAll	DC.B 04	;12 PurgeHandle	DC.B 02	;13 PurgeAll	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 04	;18 GetHandleSize	DC.B 08	;19 SetHandleSize	DC.B 04	;1A FindHandle	DC.B 00	;1B FreeMem	DC.B 00	;1C MaxBlock	DC.B 00	;1D TotalMem	DC.B 04	;1E CheckHandle	DC.B 00	;1F CompactMem	DC.B 04	;20 HLock	DC.B 02	;21 HLockAll	DC.B 04	;22 HUnlock	DC.B 02	;23 HUnlockAll	DC.B 06	;24 SetPurge	DC.B 04	;25 SetPurgeAll	DC.B 04	;26 DeRef	DC.B 00	DC.B 12	;28 PtrToHnd	DC.B 12	;29 HandToPtr	DC.B 12	;2A HandToHand	DC.B 12	;2B BlockMove	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	ENDP********************************************************************************** RDParmCnt - Parameter counts for ramdisk calls*********************************************************************************RDParmCnt	PROC	DC.B 00	;01 Boot time call	DC.B 00	;02 Application init call	DC.B 00	;03 App quit	DC.B 00	;04 Version #	DC.B 00	;05 Reset	DC.B 00	;06 Status	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	;09 Kill	DC.B 00	;0A ExecPCCall	DC.B 00	;0B SetDiskSize	DC.B 00	;0C GetDiskSize	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	DC.B 00	ENDP********************************************************************************** Vectors - This is	the defaults for the patch vectors in $E1** THE ORDER MUST BE	THE SAME AS THE EQUATES*********************************************************************************Vectors	PROC	jml XMMPatcher	jml XWarmStart	jml XLink	jml XCleanUp	jml XSearch	jml XCheckFit	jml XRealloc	jml XGetFree	jml XCreateHandles	jml XMoveData	jml XSearchFail	jml XCompact	jml XPurge	ENTRY UpDefaultUPDefault		;       	jml XUserPurge	jml XRestart	ENDP	eject********************************************************************************** RDLink - This routine is called by every RAM disk entry point*        It saves the number of parameters*        the D & B registers*        moves the stack down by ZPSize	bytes*        move the Direct register to the stack*********************************************************************************RDLink	PROC	longa on	longi on	txa	xba	sep #$30	;Into 8 bit mode	longa off	longi off	and #$FF	tax	;X = Index for parm	count	lda #$E1	;Bank reg for later	pha	lda >RDParmCnt-1,x	;Get # parameters	bra Link2	ENDP********************************************************************************** Link - This routine is called by every entry point*        It saves the number of parameters*        the D & B registers*        moves the stack down by ZPSize	bytes*        move the Direct register to the stack** Called VIA $E1 vector** Link2 entry point	from ram disk*********************************************************************************XLink	PROC	longa on	longi on	txa	xba	sep #$30	;Into 8 bit mode	longa off	longi off	and #$FF	tax	;X = Index for parm	count	lda #$E1	;Bank reg for later	pha	lda >ParmCnt-1,x	;Get number of parameters	ENTRY Link2Link2		;       	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	plx	;Save return address	ply	;and bank	and #$00FF	;Lower byte valid	pha	tsc	;Pull stack down	sec	sbc #ZPSize	tcs	phb	phd	tcd	stz retry	stz error	;Clear the error	phy	;Push RTL addr and bank	phx	jsl IncBusyFlg	;Mark us busy	plb	;B = $E1	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** CleanUp - Jumped to to exit from a tool*           It restores stack, D & B*           Pulls the parameters off off the stack*           Loads error code into A*           Sets C=1 if A <> 0** Calls goes through vector in $E1*********************************************************************************XCleanup	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl DecBusyFlg	;Open for business!	ldx numparms	;Get # params into X	lda return+4	;Move return address	sta return+4,x	lda return+2	sta return+2,x	lda return	sta return,x	tsc	;Now fix the stack	clc	adc numparms	;Stack = stack + ZP	+ parms	adc #ZPSize+5	tax	;Save it for now	pld	plb	pla	;Get error code	cmp #1	;C = 1 if <> 0	txs	;Really fix the stack	bcs ErrorExit	rtl	;Go back to userErrorExit	rtl	;Something to trigger off of	ENDP********************************************************************************** QuickExit - Quick	exit for routines not using local ZP and having no errors*********************************************************************************QuickExit	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP		Title ' Initialization stuff'********************************************************************************** Initialization routines******************************************************************************************************************************************************************* BootInit*  This is the power up call to the memory mananger*  If PowerFlag is 0, it will:*    Determine how much memory is in the computer*    Initialize all	MM constants and pointers*    Create 1K worth of pointers*    Busy out all of the areas not used	by the MM**  Caution: This call wipes the machine	and frees everything*** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Added conditional compile code below to make it possible to run the memory* manager in RAM.** 08 Jan 89	Steven Glass** Also zeroed the FirstOOMPtr so that reboot clears the OOM* queue.*********************************************************************************MMBootInit	PROC	longa on	longi on     IF RamVersion THEN	jsl XLink     ELSE; See if a true power up	lda PowerFlag	bpl NoRestart	jsl Link	jsr ClearRecent;; Clear the OOM queue.;	stz |FirstOOMPtr	stz |FirstOOMPtr+2	jsl Restart	;See if warm start	bcs PowerUp	;If failed then cold start	jml CleanupNoRestart	jsl XLink	;Vectors not set up	yet; First clear out all of our pointersPowerUp	lda #nil	ldx #MMRamEnd-MMRam-1 ;# bytes to nil outbiClear	sta |MMram,x	dex	dex	bpl biClear; Now make HandleBuf a bunch of handles	lda #50*HSize+(HandleBuf**$FFFF) ;Make 51 handles	tax; Mark This handle as next of lower handlebiLinkH	sta >$E10000-HSize+Hndl_Next,x	lda #^HandleBuf	sta >$E10000-Hsize+Hndl_Next+2,x	txa	sec	sbc #HSize	;Go down one handle; Mark this handle as previous of higher handle	tax	sta |HSize+Hndl_Prev,x	lda #^HandleBuf	sta |HSize+Hndl_Prev+2,x	txa	cmp #HandleBuf**$FFFF	;Last one?	bne biLinkH	;Go link next one; The first 6 handles go in MemList and	the rest are free	lda #nil	;Split the list between 6 & 7	sta |5*HSize+HandleBuf+Hndl_Next	sta |5*Hsize+HandleBuf+Hndl_Next+2	sta |6*HSize+HandleBuf+Hndl_Prev	sta |6*Hsize+HandleBuf+Hndl_Prev+2; Initialize FreeList, MemList, PurgeList and init Mem01 - MemFF	ldx #30SetPtr	lda >PtrInit,x	sta |MemList,x	dex	dex	bpl SetPtr; Now add the addresses and size info to the memlist segments	ldx #0	txyBusyLoop	lda >HInit,x	sta |HandleBuf+Hndl_Addr,y ;-$E1 to make orca work	lda >HInit+2,x	sta |HandleBuf+Hndl_Addr+2,y	lda >HInit+4,x	;Now the size	sta |HandleBuf+Hndl_Size,y	lda >HInit+6,x	sta |HandleBuf+Hndl_Size+2,y	lda #Attr_Locked+Attr_Fixed	sta |Handlebuf+Hndl_Attr,y ;Lock it down	txa	clc	adc #8	tax	tya	adc #HSize	tay	cmp #HSize*6	blt BusyLoop; Now fix the 4th segment for the actual amount of ram in the machine	jsr TestMem	;Get memory size	sta |HandleBuf+HSize*3+Hndl_Addr+2	txa	sta |HandleBuf+HSize*3+Hndl_Size+2    ENDIF; Initialize the vectors in $E1	ldx #VlenVectLoop	lda >Vectors,x	sta |MMPatcher,x	dex	dex	bpl VectLoop      IF RAMVersion THEN; Mark that we are up and running!	lda #FALSE	sta |PowerFlag      ELSE; Mark that we are up and running!	lda #True	sta |PowerFlag      ENDIF	jml CleanUp	;Go home; HInit - Table of initial handle data	ENTRY HInitHInit		; 	DC.L $00000000	DC.L $800	DC.L $0000C000	DC.L $00010800-$0000C000	DC.L $0001C000	DC.L $00020000-$0001C000	DC.L $00020000	DC.L $00E02000-$00020000	DC.L $00E0C000	DC.L $00E12000-$00E0C000	DC.L $00E1C000	DC.L $FFFFFFFF-$00E1C000+1; PtrInit - Table of initial values for	list pointers	ENTRY PtrInitPtrInit		; 	DC.L HandleBuf	;MemList	DC.L nil	;PurgeList	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize*6 ;FreeList	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize ;Mem01	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize*2 ;Mem02	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize*3 ;MemE0	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize*4 ;MemE1	DC.L HandleBuf+HSize*5 ;MemFF	ENDP********************************************************************************** TESTMEM - Tests the memory size*  This routine writes the complement of the bank number in	banks 2 - DF*  and then scans down until it can read one back** Outputs A: Start of unreadable banks X: Number of empty banks*********************************************************************************TestMem	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda #$0000	;Starts at $7F0000	sta addr	lda #$007F	sta addr+2	eor #$FFFFWriteLoop	sta [addr]	;Write complement in bank	dec addr+2	inc A	;Go to next bank	cmp #$FFFE	bne WriteLoop	lda #$007F	;Now read em back	sta addr+2	eor #$FFFF	ldx #$0060	;Count # unused banksTestLoop	cmp [addr]	beq GoodBank	;Found a good bank?	inx	dec addr+2	inc A	cmp #$FFFE	bne TestLoop	;Restore contentsGoodBank	lda addr+2	;Get highest readable bank	inc A	;Lowest unreadable bank	sta |NumBanks	;Save it away	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** Restart - This tests for a warm start	of the MM*              If the power up byte if 0, then it fails*              If the memory lists are inconsistent, then it fails*              If a	warm start is done then all blocks not owned by the MM*               are	disposed**           Outputs: C = 1 if warm start failed and cold start must be done** Rev 2 changes: Fixed so it doesn't dispose valid handles*********************************************************************************XRestart	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr Validate	;Check the memory lists	bne NoRestart* Get rid of all non MM blocks	jsr ScanHandles	;Mark handles that we must keep	ldx #PurgeList-MemList	jsr TrimFree	;Trim the purge list	ldx #FreeList-MemList	jsr TrimFree	jsr Start0	;Go through all used segsTrimLoop	jsr GetNext	;Hndl1 = next block	beq TrimDone	ldy #Hndl_Owner	;Get the owner	lda [Hndl1],y	bit #$FF00	;Is high byte MM	bne TrimIt	;Throw it out if not	cmp #SaveID	;Save it as free?	bne TrimLoop	dey	dey	lda [Hndl1],y	;don't dispose block of handles	bit #Attr_Handle	bne TrimLoop* The block needs to be discarded. Check if MM owns the handle!TrimIt	move_l hndl1,hndl	push_l hndl2	;Save the next handle to check	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove it from where it is	ldy #hndl_owner	lda [hndl],y	and #$FF00	;MM's?  Rev2 change.	beq KeepIt	lda hndl+2	;Is it the MMs	cmp #$00E1	bne NotMine	lda hndl	cmp #$1B00	bge NotMineKeepIt	jsr InsertFree	;Put it in free handle listNotMine	pop_l hndl2	;Get the next one to check	bra TrimLoopTrimDone	clc	rtlNoRestart	sec	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** Validate-    This	routine checks the memory lists for consistency*              For each element in the list hndl.next.prev must equal hndl**              outputs: Z = 1 if lists OK*********************************************************************************Validate	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldx #0	;Check memlist	jsr CheckList	bne Done	;Br if bad* MemList's last block should be at $E1C000. If it isn't then the list has been* fragmented and we	should cold start.	lda addr2	;Addr2 should be $00E1C000	cmp #$C000	bne Done	lda addr2+2	cmp #$00E1	bne Done	ldx #4	;Check purgelist	jsr CheckList	bne Done	;Br if bad	ldx #8	;Check freelist. Fall into CheckList* CheckList - scans	a single list	ENTRY CheckListCheckList		; 	jsr StartX	;Get start of list	beq Done	;Done if nil* For each element in list make sure that the next one points back to it* Sets Z = 0 if bad	list Z = 1 if list OKCheckLoop	jsr GetNext	beq Done	;Done if next is nil	ldy #hndl_prev	;Get previous of next	lda [hndl2],y	cmp hndl1	;Should be same as hndl1	bne Done	iny	iny	lda [hndl2],y	cmp hndl1+2	beq CheckLoop	;Loop if OKDone	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** ScanHandles - This routines scans down the list of used handles*              If it finds a block of handles, it looks if any segment*              is owned by the MM. If so, the block is preserved through reset** Revision 2 - Fix to make FFFF ID for disposed block of handles**********************************************************************************ScanHandles	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >MemList	;Look down the list	of used handles	sta Hndl	lda >MemList+2	sta Hndl+2Loop	ldy #hndl_next	;Go to the next handle	lda [Hndl],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [Hndl],y	sta Hndl+2	stx Hndl	ora Hndl+2	;Done if nil	beq Done* Check if it is a block of handles	ldy #hndl_attr	lda [Hndl],y	bit #attr_handle	beq Loop	;Br if not handles* It's a block of handles.  Check if we	have to keep any* Hndl is also the address of the block	ldy #hndl_size	;Low byte of size.	High = 0	lda [Hndl],y	sec	;Make index for owner of last one	sbc #HSize-hndl_owner	tax	;Save in X for laterKeepCheck	tay	lda [Hndl],y	;Get the owner	and #$FF00	;If High word 0 then MM own's it!	beq KeepEm	;If so, then keep them	tya	;Go down to next handle	sec	sbc #HSize	cmp #HSize	bge KeepCheck	tay	lda #$FFFF	;Mark block as disposable	sta [Hndl],y	bra Loop	;Don't keep the blockDone	rtsKeepEm	txa	;Get index to last oneKeepEm2	tay	lda [Hndl],y	;Get the owner	and #$FF00	;Does MM own it?	beq OwnerOK	;If so, leave alove	lda #SaveID	;Mark as spare to be saved	sta [Hndl],yOwnerOK	tya	;Go to next one	sec	sbc #HSize	bpl KeepEm2	bra Loop	ENDP********************************************************************************** TrimFree - Removes any non memory manager block from the free or purge list** Inputs:      X = list to trim** This routine was replaced in rev 2. Rev 1 would lose handles in $E1*********************************************************************************TrimFree	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >MemList+2,x	;Get the desired list	pha	lda >MemList,x	phaLoop	pla	;Get the handle to do	sta Hndl	pla	sta Hndl+2	ora Hndl	;Nil?	beq Done	ldy #hndl_next+2	;Get the next handle	lda [Hndl],y	;and save it on the	stack	pha	dey	dey	lda [Hndl],y	pha	ldy #hndl_owner	;If handle belongs to MM	lda [hndl],y	;then leave it where it is	cmp #$00FF	blt Loop	php	;If Z = 1 then put in free list	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove it from the	list	plp	;Did we want to save it?	beq KeepIt	;owner was 00FF	lda hndl+1	;Is it in $E11700 -	$E11AFF?	cmp #$E117	;< $E11700?	blt Loop	cmp #$E11B	;> $E11B00	bge LoopKeepIt	jsr InsertFree	;Put it in the free	list	bra LoopDone	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** MMPatcher - Used to Patch ram patches	to the MM into the tool locator*********************************************************************************XMMPatcher	PROC	longa on	longi on	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** WarmStart - called via a JSL from the	tool locator after tool initialization*********************************************************************************XWarmStart	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr ClearRecent	rtl	ENDP		Title ' Standard Calls'********************************************************************************** Standard tool calls******************************************************************************************************************************************************************* MMStartup - Application init for the memory manager** outputs:     OwnerID returned on the stack*********************************************************************************MMStartup	PROC	IMPORT GetIDOfCallingRoutine	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr GetIDOfCallingRoutine	bcc BadID	sta ParmsGetOut	jml CleanUpBadID	lda #IDErr	sta error	bra GetOut	ENDP*****************************************************************GetIDOfCallingRoutine PROC EXPORT** This little routine looks back on the stack at the routine* making a memory manager call.  It then finds what handle* that memory is contained in and returns the user ID of* the handle.*** Inputs:*	on direct page** Outputs:*	a-reg has user ID or zero*	carry set => no error*	carry clear => error*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda return+3	;Make actual return	address	clc	adc #1	sta addr	lda return+5	adc #0	and #$00FF	;High bits unused	sta addr+2	jsr Start0	;Start searching through main memoryLoop	jsr GetNext	;Scan through the blocks	beq AddrFound	cmp_l addr,addr1	;If < addr1 then in	hndl1	blt AddrFound	cmp_l addr,addr2	;If < addr2 then free	bge LoopNoOwner	lda #0	;No Owner	clc	;Indicate error	rtsAddrFound	ldy #Hndl_Owner	;Get the owner	lda [hndl1],y	bit #$F000	;Check high bits	beq NoOwner	sec	;Indicate no error	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** MMShutdown - Application shutdown*********************************************************************************MMShutdown	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	lda #<XUserPurge	;Reset the user purge routine	sta |UserPurge+1	lda #>XUserPurge	sta |UserPurge+2	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetVersion - Returns the version number*********************************************************************************MMVersion	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda #Version	;Version #	sta 7,s	jmp QuickExit	;No error	ENDP********************************************************************************** MMReset -    Called at reset*              Returns error if MM lists invalid** Change History** 08 Jan 89	Steven Glass** Also zeroed the FirstOOMPtr so that reset clears the OOM* queue.*********************************************************************************MMReset	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr ClearRecent	;zero the most recently found handles.;; Clear the OOM queue.;	stz |FirstOOMPtr	stz |FirstOOMPtr+2	jsr Validate	;Check the lists	beq Done	;Br if OK	lda #MFullErr	;Return an error	sta ErrorDone	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** Status - Returns if tool is active*********************************************************************************MMstatus	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda #true	;Return active	sta 7,s	jmp QuickExit	ENDP	title ' Creation and Dispose calls'**********************************************************************************  NewHandle - Allocate a new handle*********************************************************************************NewHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	;Fix stack etc.;;---------------------------------------------------; Last minute phone	patch from Rich applied 2 Mar 87;---------------------------------------------------	lda #$FFFF	sta Owner;---------------------------------------------------; End of last minute phone patch from Rich;---------------------------------------------------;	jsl GetFree	;Get a free handle	bcc full	;Br if err	ldx #10	;Move parametersMoveParms	lda parms,x	sta addr,x	dex	dex	bpl MoveParms	lda owner	;If owner = 0 somethings wrong	beq BadID	lda size	;Making an empty handle?	ora size+2	beq MakeEmpty	jsl Search	;Go get the segment	bcc Full	;Br if error	jsr InsertHandle	;Put handle in used	list	bra DoneBadID	lda #IDErr	;Bad owner ID	bra ErrExitFull	lda #MFullErr	;Memory Full!!!ErrExit	sta error	jsr InsertFree	;Put the handle back	stz hndl	;Return nil pointer	stz hndl+2Done	move_l hndl,ResHndl	;Return handle to caller;-----------------------------------------------------------;; As a debugging aid to those of us with Logic Analyzers,; we write the handle to a fixed location too.;	lda ResHndl	sta >NewDebugLoc	lda ResHndl+2	sta >NewDebugLoc+2;-----------------------------------------------------------	jml CleanUpMakeEmpty	lda attr	;Is it locked or anything?	bit #Attr_Locked+Attr_Fixed+Attr_Addr+Attr_Bank	beq NotLocked	;Br if OK	lda #LockErr	bra ErrExit	;Return errorNotLocked	jsr MoveAttr	;Move attributes into block	jsr InsertPurge	;Put it in the purge list	bra Done	ENDP**********************************************************************************  ReallocHandle - Creates a new handle	with a purged one*********************************************************************************ReallocHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	;Fix stack etc.	jsr VerifyHandle	;Get the inputted handle	lda [Hndl]	;Make sure addr is nil	ldy #hndl_addr+2	ora [Hndl],y	beq IsEmpty	lda #NotNilErr	;Return bad handle if not empty	sta Error	jml CleanUpIsEmpty	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove it from purged list	ldx #10	;Move parametersMoveParms	lda parms+4,x	sta addr,x	dex	dex	bpl MoveParms	lda owner	;If owner = 0 somethings wrong	beq BadID	lda size	;Making an empty handle?	ora size+2	beq MakeEmpty	jsl Search	;Go get the segment	bcc Full	;Br if error	jsr InsertHandle	;Put handle in used	list	bra DoneBadID	lda #IDErr	;Bad owner ID	bra ErrExitFull	lda #MFullErr	;Memory Full!!!ErrExit	sta errorPutPurge	jsr InsertPurge	;Put the handle backDone	jml CleanUpMakeEmpty	lda attr	;Is it locked or anything?	bit #Attr_Locked+Attr_Fixed+Attr_Addr+Attr_Bank	beq NotLocked	;Br if OK	lda #LockErr	bra ErrExit	;Return errorNotLocked	jsr MoveAttr	;Move attributes into block	bra PutPurge	ENDP********************************************************************************** RestoreHandle - used to restore a purged handle** inputs:      parmhndl - handle to be restored** Note: the handle can't be restored if	it is in a fixed bank or address*********************************************************************************RestoreHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Make sure it is a good handle	jsr GetAttr	;Get the attributes	lda addr	;Must be empty	ora addr+2	beq IsEmpty	lda #NotNilErr	;not empty!!!!!!!	bra ErrExitIsEmpty	lda attr	;Can't be fixed addr	bit #Attr_Addr+Attr_Bank	beq AttrsOK	lda #AttrErr	;Invalid attributes	bra ErrExitAttrsOK	lda size	;If size = 0, leave	it purged	ora size+2	beq Done	jsl Realloc	;Reallocate the handle	bcc Done	;Br if OK	lda #MFullErr	;Didn't workErrExit	sta ErrorDone	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** DisposHandle - Purges a handle and puts it in the FreeList** inputs:      ParmHndl: Handle to be disposed** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Added call to CheckRecent.** This compares the handle being disposed against the handle most recently* allocated and clears the variable if they are equal.*********************************************************************************DisposHandle	PROCDisposeHandle	longa on	longi on*** 12-Jun-91 DAL -- disposing the very first handle is very bad!;;MemList	equ $E11600	;List of used segments	lda 7,s	cmp >MemList	bne @notFirstHandle	lda 9,s	cmp >MemList+2	bne @notFirstHandle;;;	ldx #$0206	;bad handle error	ldx #0	;no error (19-Dec-91 DAL, to match TS2/3)	ldy #4	jml $e10184	;ToStrip (4 bytes)@notFirstHandle*** end of 12-Jun-91 DAL	jsl link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Make sure it's valid	jsr CheckRecent	;Clean up last allocated list if necessary 29 Aug 88 SEG	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove it from where it is	jsr InsertFree	;Put it in free handle list;-----------------------------------------------------------;; As a debugging aid to those of us with Logic Analyzers,; we write the handle to a fixed location too.;	lda hndl	sta >DisposeDebugLoc	lda hndl+2	sta >DisposeDebugLoc+2;-----------------------------------------------------------	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************* DisposAll - Disposes all of an owners	handles** Inputs:      parms = ownerID*** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Added call to check recent inside the loop that does the dipsosing.* This makes the check of any disposed handles against the most* recently allocated.** 06 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Changed order of two calls:  CheckRecent and RemoveHandle.  Want to * check the recent list before removing it.** 30 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Check to see of the ID of the calling routine is the same the ID passed.* If it is the same, then they are disposing of themselves, which is not * safe so we don't allow it.********************************************************************************DisposAll	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	jsr ClearRecent	;added 14-Sep-91 DAL	jsr GetIDOfCallingRoutine	cmp Parms	bne IsOK	lda #$0000	; 4/21/89 Mensch cause IDErr broke too many apps	sta Error	bra BadIDIsOK	jsr MakeIDMask	bcs BadID	;Br if bad id	jsr DoIt	;Free used handles	lda |PurgeList+2	;Now do the purged handles	tax	lda |PurgeList	jsr DoItBadID	jml CleanUp	;All done* This routine scans through a list and	frees themDoIt	jsr SearchID	;Find a matching owner in used handl	bcc Done	;Br if no more	pha	;Save a,x	phx	jsr CheckRecent	;Clean up last allocated list if necessary 29 Aug 88 SEG	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove it from where it is	jsr InsertFree	;Put it in the free	list	plx	pla	bra DoItDone	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PurgeHandle - Purges a handle** inputs:      ParmHndl: Handle to be purged** note: The handle must be unlocked and	purgeable*********************************************************************************PurgeHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	jsr VerifyHandle	jsr DoPurge	;Purge it	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************* PurgeAll - Purges	all of an owners purgeable handles** Inputs:      parms = ownerID*** Change History** 23 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Used MakeIDMask2 so that 0 can be passed as master ID.** Added stz error at AlmostDone, since none of the errors returned* mean anything and a purgeall is supposed to go purge what can* be purged and leave the rest.** 31 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Removed stz error.  Someone relied on this random error.  Verrrrry* weird, but we have to keep the Apps running.********************************************************************************PurgeAll	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	jsr ClearRecent	;added 14-Sep-91 DAL	jsr MakeIDMask2	bcs Done	;Br if bad IDLoop	jsr SearchID	;Find a matching owner	bcc Done	;Br if no more	pha	;Save a,x	phx	jsr DoPurge	;Purge it	plx	pla	bra LoopDone	jml CleanUp	;All done	ENDP********************************************************************************** DoPurge - purges a handle** Inputs: hndl = handle to be purged*********************************************************************************DoPurge	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldy #Hndl_Attr	;Get attributes of handle	lda [hndl],y	bmi IsLocked	;Br if locked	bit #Attr_Purge	;Can we purge it	beq NoPurge	;Br if level 0	jsr CheckRecent	;Clean up last allocated list if necessary 29 Aug 88 SEG	jsr RemoveHandle	jsr InsertPurge	bra DoneIsLocked	lda #LockErr	bra Done1Nopurge	lda #PurgeErrDone1	sta errorDone	rts	ENDP	title ' Information on block calls'********************************************************************************** GetHandleSize - Gets the size of a handle** inputs:      ParmHndl = Handle to get	size of** outputs:     Size	of handle*********************************************************************************GetHandleSize	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Valid handle?	geth_l Hndl,Parms+4,hndl_size ;Get the size	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** SetHandleSize - Resizes a handle*                 The handle is grown or shrunk as appropriate** Inputs:      ParmHndl = Handle to change*              Parms+4  = New size* Outputs:     none** Revision2:   Handle made unpurgable while allocating*********************************************************************************SetHandleSize	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Get and check inputted handle	jsr GetAttr	;Get the properties	of the handle	lda addr	;If addr = 0 then size must be 0	ora addr+2	bne NotNil	lda size	ora size+2	bne IsPurged	;Br if purgedNotNil	ldx size+2	;Switch new size and old	lda parms+6	stx parms+6	sta size+2	ldx size	lda parms+4	stx parms+4	sta size	sec	sbc parms+4	;Compare new size to old	tax	;Save result	lda size+2	sbc parms+6	bne IsDiff	;Is there a size change?	txa	;Was low word 0 too?	beq Done1IsDiff	bcs Grow	;Br if new > old; Here we shrink the block	lda size	;Shrink to nothing?	ora size+2	bne Not0	;Br if not	lda attr	;Can't shrink to 0 if locked	bit #Attr_Locked+Attr_Fixed+Attr_Addr+Attr_Bank	bne BadChange	;Br if can't nil it	jsr CheckRecent	;Clear Last Allocated (if necessary).	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove the handle from the used list	jsr InsertPurgeNot0	seth_l size,hndl,Hndl_Size ;Update the sizeDone1	jmp DoneIsPurged	lda #NilErr	bra Fail1BadChange	lda #LockErr	bra Fail1Fail	lda #MFullErrFail1	sta error	jmp Done; Here we grow the block	ENTRY GrowGrow		; 	lda addr	;Move present address into addr1	sta addr1	sta parms	;and into parms in case we need it	lda addr+2	;later	sta addr1+2	sta parms+2	ora addr	;Was it nil?	beq WasNil	;Br if it was; First see if we can just extend it from where it is	geth_l hndl2,addr2,hndl_addr ;Get beginning of next block* Temporarily force	Fixed so to force Bottom up check so block won't move	lda attr	pha	ora #Attr_Fixed	sta attr	jsl CheckFit	;See if it fits	pla	sta attr	;Restore actual block type	bcc NoFit	;Br if it didn't	seth_l size,hndl,Hndl_Size ;And the size	seth_l addr1,hndl,Hndl_Addr ;Update the	address	cmp addr+2	;Has the handle moved?	bne ItMoved	;Br if it did	lda addr1	;Check low word	cmp addr	beq Done1	;Do nothing if it didn't move	bra ItMoved; We have to search	for a new blockNoFit	bit attr	;Can't move it if Locked	bmi BadChange	;Br if Locked	bvs BadChange	;Br if Fixed	ENTRY WasNilWasNil		; 	ldy #Hndl_Attr	;Make unpurgable	lda attr	and #$FCFF	;Purge level 0	sta [hndl],y	jsl Search	;Go try to find one; added 21 Dec 88	lda [hndl]	; deref handle again	sta parms	; (it might have moved)	ldy #2	lda [hndl],y	sta parms+2; end addition	ldy #Hndl_Attr	;Restore purge status	lda attr	;Don't change C	sta [hndl],y	bcs @Continue	brl Fail	;Couldn't find one.	C from Search@Continue	push_l hndl1	;Save previous	jsr RemoveHandle	;Remove handle from	where it is	pop_l hndl1	;Recover where we want it to go	geth_l hndl1,hndl2,Hndl_Next ;Get where	it goes before	jsr InsertHandle	;Put it in the list; Move data that used to be in handle into new placeItMoved	move_l addr1,Dest	;Where data goes	move_l parms,Source	;Where it used to be	move_l parms+4,Count ;Old size	jsl MoveData	;Go Move itDone	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** FindHandle - Finds the handle of the block containing an address** inputs:      Parms = address** output:      handle of segment or nil	if address is free*********************************************************************************FindHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	stz parms+4	;Nil the output	stz parms+6	jsr start0	;Start at beginning	of memoryLoop	jsr GetNext	;Go to next segment	beq AddrFound	;Br if end of memory	cmp_l parms,addr1	;If < addr1 then in	hndl1	bcc AddrFound	;Br if found	cmp_l parms,addr2	;If < addr2 then in	free space	bcc AddrFree	bra LoopAddrFound	move_l hndl1,parms+4 ;Move handle to func returnAddrFree	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** FreeMem - Calculates how much free memory is in the machine** Inputs:   None** Output:   Free memory*********************************************************************************FreeMem	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	stz parms	;Clear count to 0	stz parms+2	jsr start0	;Set up a search starting from 0CountLoop	jsr GetNext	;addr1, addr2 limits of free block	beq Done	sec	;addr2 - addr1 = size of block	lda addr2	sbc addr1	tax	lda addr2+2	sbc addr1+2	tay	clc	;Now add it to total	txa	adc parms	sta parms	tya	adc parms+2	sta parms+2	bra CountLoop	;Go do the next blockDone	jml CleanUp	ENDP;;          Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1987;          All rights reserved;          Patch by	Dan Oliver;; RAM patch code to	Memory Manager.;;;;========================================================;          Return amount of allocatable	memory.;========================================================;;   IN:    No inputs.;;  OUT:    LONG - amount of RAM in system that is not allocated.;                 The amount includes unallocated and purgable.;;; Change History;; 17 May 88	Steven Glass;; Cleared carry and zeroed a-reg on exit.;;RealFreeMem	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on;;; --- Offsets into stack and direct page ---------------------------;handle	equ 1saveDirect	equ handle+4rtl1	equ saveDirect+2rtl2	equ rtl1+3totalFree	equ rtl2+3;;	phd	;Save original direct page.	pha	;Space for handle.	pha	tsc	;Switch direct page	into stack.	tcd;	stz <totalFree	;Start total free memory counter.	stz <totalFree+2;;; --- Compute size of allocated memory ------------------------------------;	lda >MemList	tax	lda >MemList+2lop1	stx <handle	sta <handle+2;	ldy #hndl_attr	;Don't count purgable blocks.	lda [<handle],y	and #attr_purge	beq CountThis	;Not purgeable so count this	lda [<handle],y	;Is purgable but may be locked so	bpl next1	;cannot be freed,  If can be freed, then;	                  ;skip.;CountThis		;	ldy #hndl_size	;Add size of this allocated block	lda [<handle],y	;to the size accumulator.	clc	adc <totalFree	sta <totalFree	iny	iny	lda [<handle],y	adc <totalFree+2	sta <totalFree+2;next1	ldy #hndl_next	lda [<handle],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<handle],y	bne lop1;;; --- From total allocated memory, subtract total memory ---------------;	lda #0	tax	sec	sbc <totalFree	sta <totalFree	txa	sbc <totalFree+2	sta <totalFree+2;	pla	;Remove temp handle.	pla	pld	;Restore direct page.	lda #0	; return no error!	clc	rtl;	ENDP********************************************************************************** MaxBlock - Finds the largest free block in the machine in	the machine** Inputs:   None** Output:   Largest	block size in parms*********************************************************************************MaxBlock	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	stz parms	;Clear size to 0	stz parms+2	jsr start0	;Set up a search starting from 0CountLoop	jsr GetNext	;addr1, addr2 limits of free block	beq Done	sec	;addr2 - addr1 = size of block	lda addr2	sbc addr1	tax	lda addr2+2	sbc addr1+2	tay	cpx parms	;Now compare it to current largest	sbc parms+2	;C = 1 if it is larger	bcc CountLoop	stx parms	;Save new largest	sty parms+2	bra CountLoop	;Go check the next blockDone	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** SetHandleID -- set the owner ID for a handle, and return the old one** Inputs:*   WORD  space for result (old ID)*   WORD  owner ID*   LONG  handle** If you pass 0 for the new ID, the old ID is unchanged, and it just tells* you what the ID is.*********************************************************************************SetHandleID	proc export	longa on	longi onoldD	equ 1rtl	equ oldD+2theHandle	equ rtl+6theNewID	equ theHandle+4theResult	equ theNewID+2	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #Hndl_Owner	lda [<theHandle],y	sta <theResult	lda <theNewID	beq @done	sta [<theHandle],y@done	pld	ldx #0	;no error	ldy #6	;strip 6 bytes	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	EndP********************************************************************************** TotalMem - Returns total memory in machine** inputs: none** output: Number of	bytes in machine including $E0 and $E1*********************************************************************************TotalMem	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	stz parms	;Low word always 0	lda |NumBanks	inc A	;Add 2 for E0, E1	inc A	sta parms+2	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** CheckHandle - Used to verify that a handle is valid** inputs:      ParmHndl = handle to verify** outputs:     none*********************************************************************************CheckHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Sets error if invalid	jml CleanUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** CompactMem - Forces memory compaction	if possible** inputs:      none** If called from an	interrupt, no compaction is done** outputs:     none*********************************************************************************CompactMem	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	lda |IrqActive	;Are we in an interrupt?	and #$00FF	bne NoCompact	;Don't compact if we are	stz Attr	;0 so all mem compacts. Rev 2	jsl CompactNoCompact	jml CleanUp	ENDP	Title ' HLock and more'********************************************************************************** HLock - Locks a handle** inputs:      ParmHndl = Handle to lock*********************************************************************************HLock	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [Hndl],y	ora #attr_locked	;Lock it	sta [Hndl],y	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** HLockAll - Locks all  handles of an owner** inputs:      Parms = Owner*********************************************************************************HLockAll	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr MakeIDMask	;Set up the mask for searching	bcs Done	;Br if bad ownerLoop	jsr SearchID	;Find a matching handle	bcc Done	;Br if no more	pha	;Save address of next one	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [hndl],y	ora #attr_locked	;Lock it	sta [hndl],y	pla	bra Loop	;Go to next oneDone	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** MakeIDMask - Sets	things up for xxxAll commands*              Parms -> owner*              Mask	 -> parms*              A,X = MemList*              C = 1 if invalid ID***********************************************************************************MakeIDMask	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda parms	bit #$F000	;Invalid mask	beq BadID	sta owner	;Get inputted owner	ora #$F000	;Build the maskJoinHere	bit #$0F00	;All aux IDs?	beq AnyAux	;Br if any	ora #$0F00AnyAux	bit #$00FF	;Any ID?	beq AnyID	ora #$00FFAnyID	sta parms	lda |MemList+2	;Get start of used segments	tax	lda |MemList	clc	rtsBadID	lda #IDErr	;Set error	sta Error	sec	rts;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Alternate entry point that does not check for a non-zero; major ID.  This is used by Purgeall so can purge all; handles at once.;	ENTRY MakeIDMask2MakeIDMask2	lda parms	sta owner	bra JoinHere	ENDP********************************************************************************** HUnlock - Unlocks	a handle** inputs:      ParmHndl = Handle to unlock*********************************************************************************HUnlock	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	;Valid handle?	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [Hndl],y	and #$7FFF	;attr_locked.EOR.$FFFF ;Unlock it	sta [Hndl],y	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** HUnlockAll - Unlocks all  handles of an owner** inputs:      Parms = Owner*********************************************************************************HUnlockAll	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr MakeIDMask	;Set up the mask for searching	bcs Done	;Br if bad idLoop	jsr SearchID	;Find a matching handle	bcc Done	;Br if no more	pha	;Save address of next one	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [hndl],y	and #$7FFF	;Unlock it	sta [hndl],y	pla	bra Loop	;Go to next oneDone	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** SetPurge - Sets the purge level of a block** inputs:      ParmHndl = Handle to lock*              Parms+4  = New purge Level*********************************************************************************SetPurge	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	jsr VerifyHandle	lda parms+4	;Get new purge level	and #3	;Only want 2 bits	xba	;Move em to where they go	sta parms+4	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [Hndl],y	and #$FCFF	;Mask out purge bits	ora parms+4	;Or in new level	sta [Hndl],y	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** SetPurgeAll - Sets the purge level of	all of an owners blocks** inputs:      Parms = Owner*              Parms+2 = New purge level*********************************************************************************SetPurgeAll	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl Link	lda parms+2	;Get new purge level	and #3	;Only want 2 bits	xba	;Move em to where they go	sta parms+2	jsr MakeIDMask	;Set up the mask for searching	bcs Done	;Br if bad ownerLoop	jsr SearchID	;Find a matching handle	bcc Done	;Br if no more	pha	;Save address of next one	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get attributes byte for handle	lda [hndl],y	and #$FCFF	;Mask off purge bits	ora parms+2	;Put in new ones	sta [hndl],y	pla	bra Loop	;Go to next oneDone	jml Cleanup	ENDP********************************************************************************** PtrToHand - Moves	a block of data from an address to a handle** Inputs:      parms = Number of bytes to move*              parms+4 = Destination handle*              parms+8 = Source address*********************************************************************************PtrToHand	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	lda parms+4	;Check the handle	sta hndl	lda parms+6	sta hndl+2	jsr VerifyH2	move_l Parms,Count	;Get the parameters	lda [parms+4]	;Get dest address	sta Dest	ldy #hndl_addr+2	lda [parms+4],y	sta Dest+2	ora Dest	;If Nil then error	beq IsNil	move_l Parms+8,Source	jsl MoveData	;Go do itDone	jml CleanUpIsNil	lda #NilErr	;Can't copy to nil handle	sta error	bra Done	ENDP********************************************************************************** HandToPtr - Moves	a block of data from a handle to an address** Inputs:      parms = Number of bytes to move*              parms+4 = Destination address*              parms+8 = Source handle*********************************************************************************HandToPtr	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	lda parms+8	;Check the handle	sta hndl	lda parms+10	sta hndl+2	jsr VerifyH2	move_l Parms,Count	;Get the parameters	move_l Parms+4,Dest	lda [parms+8]	;Get source address	sta Source	ldy #hndl_addr+2	lda [parms+8],y	sta Source+2	ora Source	;If Nil then error	beq IsNil	jsl MoveData	;Go do itDone	jml CleanUpIsNil	lda #NilErr	;Can't copy to nil handle	sta error	bra Done	ENDP********************************************************************************** HandToHand - Moves a block of data from a handle to a handle** Inputs:      parms = Number of bytes to move*              parms+4 = Destination handle*              parms+8 = Source handle*********************************************************************************HandToHand	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	lda parms+4	;Check the destination handle	sta hndl	lda parms+6	sta hndl+2	jsr VerifyH2	lda parms+8	;Check the source handle	sta hndl	lda parms+10	sta hndl+2	jsr VerifyH2	move_l Parms,Count	;Get the parameters	lda [parms+4]	;Get dest address	sta Dest	ldy #hndl_addr+2	lda [parms+4],y	sta Dest+2	ora Dest	;If Nil then error	beq IsNil	lda [parms+8]	;Get source address	sta Source	lda [parms+8],y	;Y = 2 from earlier	sta Source+2	ora Source	;If Nil then error	beq IsNil	jsl MoveData	;Go do itDone	jml CleanUpIsNil	lda #NilErr	;Can't copy to nil handle	sta error	bra Done	ENDP********************************************************************************** BlockMove - Moves	a block of data** Inputs:      parms = Number of bytes to move*              parms+4 = Destination address*              parms+8 = Source address*********************************************************************************BlockMove	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl link	move_l Parms,Count	;Get the parameters	move_l Parms+4,Dest	move_l Parms+8,Source	jsl MoveData	;Go do it	jml CleanUp	ENDP	title ' Allocation routines'********************************************************************************** Search - Searches	for a segment that fits the current parameters*          note: segment is found but handle is not inserted*          SearchUp	& SearchDown are used for low to high and high to low*          allocation** inputs:      segment attributes** outputs:     C=1 if segment found C=0	if no fit** calls to search go through $E1** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Now trys calls SearchUpFast and SearchDownFast.  These routines* can find a space for a handle faster than the SearchDown and SearchUp* (but can lead to more fragmentation).*********************************************************************************XSearch	PROC	longa on	longi on	inc |NewHandleCount	bne @NoCarry	inc |NewHandleCount+2@NoCarry	lda attr	;Check the attributes	bit #attr_addr	;User's address?	beq NotAddr	;Br if not	ora #attr_fixed+attr_bank ;Force these	sta attrNotAddr	bit #attr_fixed	;Movable block?	bne @KeepLooking	jmp SearchDownFast	;If not fixed, do top down@KeepLooking	bit #attr_handle	;Allocating a handle	beq SearchUp	;If so fall into searchhandle	ENDP********************************************************************************** SearchHandle This	is used to search from low to high memory for a handle*              The search order is:*                  Bank $E0 to $FF (slow memory)*                  Bank $01 to $DF (in SearchUp)** outputs:     C=1 if segment found C=0	if no fit*********************************************************************************SearchHandle	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	ldx #MemE0-Memlist	jsr StartX	;X says where to start fromLoopE0	jsr GetNextFree	;Go to next free segment	beq Failed	;Br if nil	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc LoopE0	rtlFailed	lda attr	;Fall into SearchUp	ENDP********************************************************************************** SearchUp     This	is used to search from low to high memory*              The search order is:*                  Bank $01 to $E0*                  Bank $E0 to $FF (slow memory)*                  Bank 0** inputs:      attributes in A & attr** outputs:     C=1 if segment found C=0	if no fit** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** When a handle is found, we remember it in LastLowhHandle.*********************************************************************************SearchUp	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	ldx #Mem01-Memlist	;Assume starting from bank1	bit #attr_bank	;Fixed bank?	beq BankOk	;Br if not	lda addr+2	;Which bank?	beq Search0	;Br if bank 0	cmp #$E0	;Bank E0 or E1?	bcc BankOk	;Br if 1 to DF	ldx #MemE0-Memlist** Search $01 to $FF	or $E0 to $FF if fixed in $E0 or $E1*BankOk	jsr StartX	;X says where to start fromLoop01	jsr GetNextFree	;Go to next free segment	beq Search0	;Br if nil	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc Loop01	lda attr	;don't remember this one if its fixed bank or fixed addr	bit #attr_bank	bne ForgetThisOne	bit #Attr_Addr	bne ForgetThisOne	lda hndl	; put handle into place	sta |LastLowHandle	lda hndl+2	sta |LastLowHandle+2ForgetThisOne	rtl** Search0 - Searches bank 0*	ENTRY Search0Search0		; 	jsr Start0	;Set up to start searchLoop00	jsr GetNextFree	;Go to next free segment	lda addr1+2	;Past bank0?	bne GiveUp	;Br if true	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc Loop00	rtlGiveUp	jsl SearchFail	;C = 0 for failed	bcc GiveUp2	jmp XSearchGiveUp2	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** SearchDown   This	is used to search from high to low memory*              The search order is:*                  Bank $DF to $01*                  Bank $FF to $E0 (slow memory)*                  Bank 0** inputs:      attributes in A & attr** outputs:     C=1 if segment found C=0	if no fit*** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** When a handle is found, we remember it in LastHighHandle.*********************************************************************************SearchDown	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	bit #attr_bank	;Fixed bank?	beq BankOk	;Br if not	lda addr+2	;Which bank?	beq Search00	;Br if bank 0	cmp #$E0	;Bank E0 or E1?	bcs SearchFF	;Br if so** Search $DF to $01*BankOk	ldx #MemE0-Memlist	;Start from bank $DF	jsr StartXTop	;X says where to start fromLoopDF	jsr GetPrevFree	;Go to next lower free segment	lda addr1+2	;If bank 0 DF - 1 done	beq SearchFF	;Br if nil	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc LoopDF	lda attr	;don't remember this one if its fixed bank or fixed addr	bit #attr_bank	bne ForgetThisOne	bit #Attr_Addr	bne ForgetThisOne	lda hndl	; put handle into place	sta |LastHighHandle	lda hndl+2	sta |LastHighHandle+2ForgetThisOne	rtl** Search $FF to $E0	(Really $E1 and $E0)*SearchFF	ldx #MemFF-Memlist	;Start from bank $FF	jsr StartXTop	;X says where to start fromLoopFF	jsr GetPrevFree	;Go to next lower free segment	lda addr1+2	;Done if past $E0	cmp #$00E0	blt Search00	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc LoopFF	rtl** Search00 - Searches bank 0*	ENTRY Search00Search00		; 	ldx #Mem01-Memlist	jsr StartXTop	;Set up to start searchLoop00	jsr GetPrevFree	;Go to next free segment	beq GiveUp	;Br if nil	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc Loop00	rtlGiveUp	jsl SearchFail	;C = 0 for failed	bcc GiveUp2	jmp XSearchGiveUp2	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** SearchDownFast*              This	is used to search from high to low memory*              The search order is:*                  Starting with last handle found, *                  Bank $DF to $01*                  Bank $FF to $E0 (slow memory)*                  Bank 0** inputs:      attributes in A & attr** outputs:     C=1 if segment found C=0	if no fit** Change History** 30 Aug 88	Steven Glass** Added this routine to speed up the search for space for a new* handle.  This routine starts from the last allocated handle* rather than from the beginning or the end of the list.** This code was created by starting with SearchUp and removing* all the code that was used if the first try failed.  This* routine only handles fixed blocks that are not in a particular* bank.** If we fail at finding what we want, we return control to the * original SearchUp code.  This means that we won't return* memory full if there is an available gap after the* last allocated handle.** When a handle is found, we remember it in LastHighHandle.*********************************************************************************SearchDownFast	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	bit #attr_bank	;Fixed bank?	bne TryOldWay	lda |LastHighHandle+2	beq TryOldWay	sta hndl1+2	lda |LastHighHandle	sta hndl1LoopDF	jsr GetPrevFree	;Go to next lower free segment	lda addr1+2	;If bank 0 DF - 1 done	beq TryOldWay	;Br if nil	jsl CheckFit	;Will it fit?	bcc LoopDF	lda attr	;if the handle was at a fixed location, don't	bit #Attr_Addr	;remember it.	bne ForgetThisOne	lda hndl	; put handle into place	sta |LastHighHandle	lda hndl+2	sta |LastHighHandle+2ForgetThisOne	inc |ShortCutCount	bne @NoCarry	inc |ShortCutCount+2@NoCarry	rtlTryOldWay	lda attr	jmp SearchDown	ENDP********************************************************************************** Start0 - Sets everything up to start a search from bank0** StartX - Uses X as an index from MemList for where to start from** Output - Z = 1 if	empty list*********************************************************************************Start0	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	ldx #0	;Use MemList	ENTRY StartXStartX		;       	lda |MemList,x	;Get where to start	from	sta hndl2	lda |MemList+2,x	sta hndl2+2	;nil if = 0	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** StartXtop-  Uses X as an index from MemList for where to start from*             Sets up for top down search** Output - Z = 1 if	empty list*********************************************************************************StartXTop	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda |MemList,x	;Get where to start	from	sta hndl1	lda |MemList+2,x	sta hndl1+2	;nil if = 0	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** BestTop - Gets the best top for a top	down search*              If Fixed Bank 0, then X = Mem01 - MemList*              If Fixed Bank 1, then X = Mem02 - MemList*              Else	X = MemFF - MemList** OutPuts:     X*********************************************************************************BestTop	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldx #MemFF-MemList	;Assume not fixed	lda attr	;Get Attributes	bit #Attr_Bank	;Check for fixed bank	beq NotFixed	;Br if not	lda addr+2	;Get bank	beq IsBank0	;Bank 0?	lsr A	bne NotFixed	;Br if not bank 1	ldx #Mem02-MemListNotFixed	rtsIsBank0	ldx #Mem01-MemList	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** CHECKFIT - This routine is used to test if a segment will	fit between*            two addresses** The following attributes are checked:	fixed address, fixed bank,* page aligned, special memory, and bank crossing** If the fixed bit is clear, then segment is allocated from	the top*** Inputs  addr1: beginning address*         addr2: ending address*         size : number of bytes in segment*         attr : attributes of segment** Outputs C = 0 if doesn't fit*           = 1 if segment fits*         addr1: beginning address to allocate (may be different from input)*         addr2  destroyed*         size, attr unchanged** Calls go through $E1** Modified by Konstantin Othmer on Nov. 11, 88**     Added check at beginning for attributes.  If there are none (the most common*       case) we branch directly to check part.*********************************************************************************XCheckFit	PROC	longa on	longi on; If addr1 = addr2 then don't bother;	lda addr1;	cmp addr2;	bne AddrOK;	lda addr1+2;	cmp addr2+2;	bne AddrOK;NoFit	clc;	rtlAddrOK	lda attr	;Get search attributes	and #$7CFF	;strip off purge and locked	bne Cont1	;top down, no attributes	brl Check2Cont1	cmp #$4000	bne Cont2	;Bottom up no attributes	brl CheckCont2	lda attr;; Check if fixed bank;	lsr A	bcc AddChk	;Br if don't care	tay	cmp_w addr2+2,addr+2 ;If addr2 bank < addr bank then no fit	bcc NoFit2	cmp_w addr+2,addr1+2 ;If addr bank < addr1 bank then no fit	bcc NoFit2	beq SameBank	;Br if bank was ok	sta addr1+2	;Set addr1 to beginning of bank	stz addr1SameBank	tya; Check if rest of address fixed tooAddChk	lsr A	bcc PageChk	;If this true, bank	was too	tay	cmp_l addr2,addr	;If addr2 < addr then no fit	bcc NoFit	cmp_w addr,addr1	;If addr < addr1 then no fit	bcc NoFit	;We know that bank is ok	sta addr1	;Set addr1 = addr	tya; Check if page alignment needed. 4th byte of addr1 ignoredPageChk	lsr A	;C = 1 if aligned	bit attr	;If top down search	bvc SpecChk	; then page check done later	bcc SpecChk	;Br if don't care	tay	;Save attributes	lda #$FF	trb addr1	;Force Alignment	beq AlignOk	;Br if was aligned	inc addr1+1	;Carry into bytes 2	& 3	cmp_w addr2+1,addr1+1 ;If addr2 < addr1	then no fitNoFit2	bcc NoFitAlignOk	tya	;Get attr back; Now Check for special memory ok; Note: if one address if in special memory, the other will	be in the same bankSpecChk	lsr A	;C = 1 if can't use	special	bcc BankChk	;Br if don't care	ldy addr2+2	;If addr2 in special then give up	cpy #2	;Banks 0 & 1 special	bcc NoFit	ldx #$5FFF	;Bank E0 up to $6000 special	cpy #$E0	;If 1 < bank < E0 then ok	blt BankChk	beq IsE0	;Br if bank E0	ldx #$9FFF	;Bank E1 up to $A000 specialIsE0	cpx addr1	;Is addr1 not special?	bcc BankChk	;We're not in special if it isn't	cpx addr2	;Is addr2 not special?	bcs NoFit	;Give up if it is special	inx	;Make addr1 first non special byte	stx addr1; Now check if bank	crossing allowed.; If not, separate segment into smaller	segmentsBankChk	lsr A	;C = 1 if can't cross bank	bit attr	bvc BankChk2	;Br to top down routines	bcc Check	;Br if don't careBankLoop	cmp_w addr2+2,addr1+2 ;Same bank?	beq Check	pha	;A = addr2+2 from macro	push_w addr2	;Save addr2	stz addr2	;Make addr2 bottom of next bank	lda addr1+2	inc A	sta addr2+2	jsl Check	bcs Found	;Br if it fit	move_l addr2,addr1	;Move addr2 to addr1	pop_l addr2	;Restore addr2	bra BankLoop	;Try again from hereFound	pla	;Get rid of saved addr2	pla	rtlNoFit	clc	rtl; Now see if addr2 - addr1 >= size.Check	sec	lda addr2	;Y,A = addr2 - addr1	sbc addr1	tay	lda addr2+2	sbc addr1+2	cpy size	sbc size+2	;C = 0 if no fit	rtl* These routines are for allocating from the topBankChk2	bcc Check2	;Br if bank cross OK	cmp_w addr1+2,addr2+2 ;Does the free space cross a bank?	beq Check2	;Br if in same bank	pha	;Save addr1. A = addr1+2 from cmp_w	push_w addr1	stz addr1	;Set addr1 to beginning of bank	lda addr2+2	; containing addr2BankLoop2	sta addr1+2	;Save starting address for this try	jsl Check2	;Does it fit?	bcs Found	;Cleanup stack and return if so.	lda addr1	;Make addr2 end of next lower bank	sta addr2	lda addr1+2	sta addr2+2	dec A	;Move A down to next bank	cmp 3,s	;Are we in the original addr1 bank?	bne BankLoop2	;If so, this is last check.	pop_l addr1	;Restore original addr1* If addr2-size >= addr1 then the segment fits and the starting address* is addr2-size.  Page alignment is also done hereCheck2	sec	;Calc addr2-size	lda addr2	sbc size	tax	;X = low word	lda attr	;Force page alignment	and #Attr_Page	;Don't alter C!	beq PageOK	txa	and #$FF00	;Force to lower page	taxPageOK	lda addr2+2	sbc size+2	bcc Done	;No good if size > addr2	tay	;Y = high word	cpx addr1	;Is result < addr1?	sbc addr1+2	bcc Done	;Br with C=0 if failed	stx addr1	;Hooray! save starting address in addr1	sty addr1+2	;and return with C = 0Done	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** SearchID - Searches for a handle owned by owner** Inputs:      A,X = First handle of list to check** Outputs:     C = 0 if none found and end of list*              Hndl	= Handle found*              A,X = next handle in list*********************************************************************************SearchID	PROC	longa on	longi on	clc	;Assume nilLoop	sta hndl	;Store the handle	stx hndl+2	ora hndl+2	;Was it nil?	beq IsNil	ldy #Hndl_Owner	;Get the owner	lda [hndl],y	and parms	;And it with mask	cmp owner	;Is it who we want?	beq Found	;C=1 if found	clc	;Mark not foundFound	ldy #Hndl_Next+2	;Get the next one	lda [hndl],y	tax	;X = high	dey	dey	lda [hndl],y	;A = low	bcc Loop	;Go to next if not foundIsNil	rts	;C = 1 if found	ENDP	title ' Handle Manipulation Stuff'********************************************************************************** InsertHandle - Inserts a handle into the used memory list** MoveAttr - moves the attributes into a handle*********************************************************************************InsertHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	seth_l hndl,hndl1,hndl_next ;This is the next from hndl1	seth_l hndl,hndl2,hndl_prev ;This is the previous from hndl2	move_l addr1,addr	;Move the starting address	ENTRY MoveAttrMoveAttr		;       	ldy #HSize-2	;Move the data into	the handlemoveloop	tyx	lda addr,x	sta [hndl],y	dey	dey	bpl moveloop	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetAttr - Gets the attributes of a handle** Inputs:      hndl:    handle to get info from** Outputs:     zp:	    handle data*********************************************************************************GetAttr	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldy #HSize-2	;Get the data from the handlemoveloop	tyx	lda [hndl],y	sta addr,x	dey	dey	bpl moveloop	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** ReAlloc - reallocates a handle** Inputs:      hndl	= handle to reallocate** Outputs:     C = 1 if failed*              zp has handle attributes** Calls go through $E1 vector*********************************************************************************XRealloc	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr GetAttr	;Get the attributes	lda addr	ora addr+2	;Is it really nil?	bne NotNil	;Can't realloc if not nil	jsr RemoveHandle	jsl Search	bcc Full	jsr InsertHandle	;Put it in used list	clc	rtlFull	jsr InsertPurge	;Put it back in purge listNotNil	sec	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** RemoveHandle - Removes a handle from a list*                If	hndl.next <> nil then hndl.next.prev = hndl.prev*                If	hndl.prev <> nil then hndl.prev.next = hndl.next* Inputs:      hndl	= handle to be removed*              hndl1, hndl2 used*********************************************************************************RemoveHandle	PROC	longa on	longi on	geth_l hndl,hndl1,hndl_prev ;Get previous handle	geth_l hndl,hndl2,hndl_next ;and the next too	lda hndl2	;Is next nil?	ora hndl2+2	beq IsNil	;Br if it is	seth_l hndl1,hndl2,hndl_prev ;Set previous of next handleIsNil	lda hndl1	;Is previous nil	ora hndl1+2	beq Head	;If so, head of a list	seth_l hndl2,hndl1,hndl_next	rtsHead	ldx #FreeList-MemList ;Check if head of	free or purge	lda hndl	cmp |FreeList	bne NotFree	lda hndl+2	cmp |FreeList+2	beq IsFreeNotFree	lda hndl	;Head of purged list	cmp |PurgeList	bne NotPurge	lda hndl+2	cmp |PurgeList+2	bne NotPurge	ldx #PurgeList-MemListIsFree	lda hndl2	;Make hndl2 head of	list	sta |MemList,x	lda hndl2+2	sta |MemList+2,xNotPurge	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetFree - Gets the next free handle from the free list**           Outputs: hndl = free handle*	 Z = 1 if no free handles** Goes through $E1 vector*********************************************************************************XGetFree	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda |FreeList	;Get pointer to free handles	sta hndl	lda |FreeList+2	sta hndl+2	ora hndl	;Nil pointer?	bne HndlOk; Try to allocate more handles	lda #50	;Make 50 handles	jsl CreateHandles	;Go make them	bcc Done	;Br if error	jsr InsertFrBlock	;Put them in free list	bra XGetFree	;Go try againHndlOK	ldy #hndl_next	;Get the next handle	lda [hndl],y	sta hndl1	;Put it in hndl1 and freelist	sta |FreeList	iny	iny	lda [hndl],y	sta |FreeList+2	sta hndl1+2	ora hndl1	;Was it nil?	beq nomore	lda #nil	;Make its previous nil	ldy #hndl_prev	sta [hndl1],y	iny	iny	sta [hndl1],ynomore	sec	;No errordone	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** InsertFree - Inserts a handle into the free list**              hndl.next = (FreeList)*              hndl.prev = nil*              rest	of handle zeroed*              FreeList = (hndl)** Inputs:      hndl	= handle to be inserted*              Y = Size of block for DoInsert*********************************************************************************InsertFree	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldy #HSize	;Do one handle	ldx #FreeList-MemList ;Point to free list	ENTRY DoInsertDoInsert		;       	lda hndl+2	;Don't do it if bad	handle	beq Done	phy	;Save Size for later	dey	;Link rest of list to this one	dey	;Point to hndl.next	lda |MemList+2,x	sta [hndl],y	sta hndl2+2	;Save it for later	dey	dey	lda |MemList,x	sta [hndl],y	sta hndl2	lda hndl	;Make this handle the first one	sta |MemList,x	lda hndl+2	sta |MemList+2,x	lda #nil	;Zero out other stuff	ldy #hndl_prev+2	;Now set the previous	sta [hndl],y	;Previous = nil	dey	dey	sta [hndl],y	ldy #Hndl_Addr	;Address = nil	sta [hndl],y	iny	iny	sta [hndl],y; Set hndl2.prev to	hndl+blocksize-HSize	pla	;Recover block size	ldy hndl2+2	;Is hndl2 nil?	beq Done	;If so, there is no	next	ldy #hndl_prev	sec	sbc #HSize	clc	adc hndl	sta [hndl2],y	iny	iny	lda hndl+2	adc #0	sta [hndl2],yDone	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** InsertFrBlock  Inserts a free block of handles*********************************************************************************InsertFrBlock	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldx #FreeList-MemList ;Point to free list	ENTRY DoBlockInsertDoBlockInsert		;       	tya	;Get rid of first handle	sec	sbc #HSize	tay	lda hndl	;Move hndl up by one	clc	adc #HSize	sta hndl	lda hndl+2	adc #0	sta hndl+2	jmp DoInsert	ENDP********************************************************************************** InsertPgBlock - Inserts a block of empty handles** Inputs:      hndl	= Block of handles (first one is skipped)*              Y = size of block in bytes** Outputs:     hndl	points to first empty handle*********************************************************************************InsertPgBlock	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldx #PurgeList-MemList ;Point to free list	bra DoBlockInsert	ENDP********************************************************************************** InsertPurge - Inserts a handle into PurgeList*********************************************************************************InsertPurge	PROC	longa on	longi on	ldy #HSize	;Do one block	ldx #PurgeList-MemList	bra DoInsert	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetNext - Goes to	the next segment in	the list*              hndl2 -> hndl1*              hndl1.next -> hndl2*              hndl1.addr+hndl1.size-> addr1*              hndl2.addr -> addr2*              if hndl2 = nil then Z = 1 and addr2 unchanged** GetPrev - Goes to	the previous segment in the list*              hndl1 -> hndl2*              hndl2.prev -> hndl1*              hndl1.addr+hndl1.size-> addr1*              hndl2.addr -> addr2*              if hndl2 = nil then Z = 1 and addr2 unchanged*********************************************************************************GetNext	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi off	sep #$10	;8 bit index	move_l hndl2,hndl1	;hndl1 = hndl2	ldy #hndl_next	;hndl2 = hndl1.next	lda [hndl1],y	sta hndl2	ldy #hndl_next+2	lda [hndl1],y	sta hndl2+2	beq Done	;Br if hndl2 nil	bra NotNil	ENTRY GetPrevGetPrev		;       	sep #$10	;8 bit index	move_l hndl1,hndl2	;hndl2 = hndl1	ldy #hndl_prev	;hndl1 = hndl2.prev	lda [hndl2],y	sta hndl1	ldy #hndl_prev+2	lda [hndl2],y	sta hndl1+2	beq Done	;Br if hndl1 nilNotNil	ldy #hndl_size	;addr1 = addr+size	clc	lda [hndl1],y	adc [hndl1]	;add addr	sta addr1	ldy #hndl_size+2	lda [hndl1],y	ldy #hndl_addr+2	adc [hndl1],y	sta addr1+2	lda [hndl2],y	;addr2 = hndl2.addr	sta addr2+2	;Y = hndl_addr+2 from earlier	lda [hndl2]	sta addr2	iny	;Make Z <> 1Done	rep #$10	;Back to 16 bit X	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetNextFree - Goes to the next free segment in the list*              hndl2 -> hndl1*              hndl1.next -> hndl2*              hndl1.addr+hndl1.size-> addr1*              hndl2.addr -> addr2*              if hndl2 = nil then Z = 1 and addr2 unchanged** GetPrev - Goes to	the previous free segment in the list*              hndl1 -> hndl2*              hndl2.prev -> hndl1*              hndl1.addr+hndl1.size-> addr1*              hndl2.addr -> addr2*              if hndl2 = nil then Z = 1 and addr2 unchanged** Returns with equal flag set if next handle is nil.**  Added by Konstantin Othmer Nov. 11, 88*********************************************************************************GetNextFree	PROC	longa on	longi off	sep #$10	;8 bit index	move_l hndl2,hndl1	;hndl1 = hndl2	ldy #hndl_next	;hndl2 = hndl1.next	lda [hndl1],y	sta hndl2	ldy #hndl_next+2	lda [hndl1],y	sta hndl2+2	beq Done	;Br if hndl2 nilNotNil	ldy #hndl_size	;addr1 = addr+size	clc	lda [hndl1],y	adc [hndl1]	;add addr	sta addr1	ldy #hndl_size+2	lda [hndl1],y	ldy #hndl_addr+2	adc [hndl1],y	sta addr1+2	lda [hndl2],y	;addr2 = hndl2.addr	sta addr2+2	;Y = hndl_addr+2 from earlier	lda [hndl2]	sta addr2; If addr1 = addr2 then skip get the next one	cmp addr1	bne AddrOK	lda addr1+2	cmp addr2+2	bne AddrOKNoFit	bra GetNextFreeAddrOK	iny	;Make Z <> 1Done	rep #$10	;Back to 16 bit X	rts	ENTRY GetPrevFreeGetPrevFree		;       	sep #$10	;8 bit index	move_l hndl1,hndl2	;hndl2 = hndl1	ldy #hndl_prev	;hndl1 = hndl2.prev	lda [hndl2],y	sta hndl1	ldy #hndl_prev+2	lda [hndl2],y	sta hndl1+2	beq Done	;Br if hndl1 nil	ldy #hndl_size	;addr1 = addr+size	clc	lda [hndl1],y	adc [hndl1]	;add addr	sta addr1	ldy #hndl_size+2	lda [hndl1],y	ldy #hndl_addr+2	adc [hndl1],y	sta addr1+2	lda [hndl2],y	;addr2 = hndl2.addr	sta addr2+2	;Y = hndl_addr+2 from earlier	lda [hndl2]	sta addr2;; If addr1 = addr2 then skip get the next one;	cmp addr1	bne AddrOK	lda addr1+2	cmp addr2+2	bne AddrOK	bra GetPrevFree	ENDP	title ' Handle Creation'********************************************************************************** CreateHandles - Makes a bunch of handles** Inputs:      A = # handles to make max of 3275 ( one banks worth )** Outputs:     C = 0 if unable to allocate handles*              Y = Size of block in bytes** Note: addr through addr2 are destroyed** Calls go through $E1 vector** Revision 2 change: Block is allocated	with the id $00FF*	 Handles in free list have ID $FFFF*********************************************************************************XCreateHandles	PROC	longa on	longi on; First create a block to hold the handles	inc A	;Add 1 for segment holding rest	asl A	;Mult A by 20. 4 * A + 16 * A	asl A	sta size	;Temp	asl A	asl A	adc size	sta size	;This is the size to allocate	stz size+2	lda #Attr_Locked+Attr_Fixed+Attr_Handle+Attr_NoSpec	sta attr	jsr Search	;Go find one	bcc Full	;Oh no!	move_l addr1,hndl	;The first one is used to hold them all	jsr InsertHandle	;Put it in used list	lda #$00FF	;Make owner id $00FF	ldy #Hndl_Owner	sta [hndl],y; Now clear the handle info.  Hndl = beginning address of segment	move_w size,addr1	;and the size (high	word 0)	stz addr	;Zero them out for free handles	stz addr+2	stz attr	stz size	stz size+2;;---------------------------------------------------; Last minute phone	patch from Rich at 2 Mar 87; These lines are now in NewHandle;---------------------------------------------------;              lda	    #$FFFF;              sta	    owner;---------------------------------------------------; End of Last minute phone patch from Rich;---------------------------------------------------;; Now link them all	together	ldy #HSize	;Start at the first	one	ENTRY DoHandleDoHandle		; ; Calc previous handle	tya	;Previous = hndl+Y-20	sec	sbc #HSize	;No borrow possible	clc	adc hndl	sta hndl1	lda hndl+2	adc #0	sta hndl1+2; Calc next handle	tya	;Next = hndl+Y+20	clc	adc #HSize	;Carry don't care	clc	adc hndl	sta hndl2	lda hndl+2	adc #0	sta hndl2+2; Move all of the bytes into the handle	ldx #0DoByte	lda addr,x	sta [hndl],y	iny	iny	inx	inx	cpx #HSize	;Done all of handle?	blt DoByte	cpy addr1	;If Y = size then done	blt DoHandle	;Exit with C = 1Full	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** VerifyHandle - Veriifies that an inputted handle is a real handle*              to be valid:*              Hndl	<> nil*              Hndl.prev.next = hndl or	nil*              if hndl.prev.next = nil then hndl must be head of a list** inputs:      ParmHndl = handle to check** outputs:     Hndl	= handle*              if invalid, return address popped and jumps to CleanUp** VerifyH2 entry point from move routines Checks Z flag*********************************************************************************VerifyHandle	PROC Export	longa on	longi on	lda ParmHndl	;Get the inputted handle	sta Hndl	lda ParmHndl+2	sta Hndl+2	ENTRY VerifyH2VerifyH2		;       	beq BadHandle	;If 0 then no good	ldy #Hndl_Prev	;Get the previous	lda [hndl],y	sta hndl1	iny	iny	lda [hndl],y	sta hndl1+2	ora hndl1	;Is there no previous?	beq NoPrev; ###; Mensch 11/13/89; Add test here to see if prev and Next are the same in Hndl; This will detect if a handle was "echo" of the data bank register in high RAM;	ldy #Hndl_Next	; get the next of the same handle...	lda [Hndl],y	cmp Hndl1	; see if the low word is the same	bne @passSubTest	; if not then it passes this test...	iny	iny	lda [Hndl],y	cmp hndl1+2	bne @passSubTest	bra BadHandle	; else this is a bad handle...;@PassSubTest; ###	ldy #Hndl_Next	;Get the next of the previous	lda [Hndl1],y	cmp Hndl	;Is it = hndl?	bne BadHandle	iny	iny	lda [Hndl1],y	cmp Hndl+2	bne BadHandleHandleOK	rts	;It was OKNoPrev	ldx #FreeList-MemList ;Head of a list?HeadLoop	lda hndl	cmp MemList,x	bne NotHead	lda hndl+2	cmp MemList+2,x	beq HandleOK	;We Found itNotHead	dex	dex	dex	dex	bpl HeadLoop	;Go try next listBadHandle	lda #HandleErr	;Give back error	sta Error	pla	;Pop return address	jmp CleanUp	ENDP	title ' BlockMove Routines'********************************************************************************** MoveData - Moves a block of data with	multiple MVN or MVP	operations** Inputs:      Source: Source address*              Dest:   Destination address*              Count:  # Bytes to move** Note No address checking is done to make sure move doesn't crash machine* The code for the move is pushed on the stack** Rev 2 change: High byte of 4 byte address masked off*** Call goes through	$E1 vector*********************************************************************************XMoveData	PROC	longa on	longi on* Dec Count by 1 and return if no bytes	to move	lda Count	bne NoBor	;If 0 borrow from high byte	dec Count+2	;Dec high word	bpl NoBor	;0 bytes to move?	rtl	;Br if soNoBor	dec Count* Check if source >= Destination	ldx Source	;Low word of source	cpx Dest	;Do the compare	lda Source+2	;Now the high word	sbc Dest+2	;C = 1 if Source >=	Dest	bcs MoveDown********************************************************************************** MoveUP* This is used if Source <  Destination* inputs: X = >Source C = 0*********************************************************************************	ENTRY MoveUpMoveUp		; * Adjust Source = Source + Count and Dest = Dest + Count* Put move code in mem: MVP dst src RTL	txa	adc Count	;C = 0 from entry	tax	lda Source+2	;Get Source bank	adc Count+2	;A = 00bank	and #$00FF	;Ignore high byte	ora #$6B00	;RTL Opcode C = 0	pha	;Put it on the stack	lda Count	;Calc Dest + Count	sta TempCount	;We'll need this later	adc Dest	tay	lda Count+2	adc Dest+2	;A = 00bank	xba	;A = bank00	ora #$44	;MVP opcode	pha	bra muFirstMuMore	sta Count+2	;More bytes to move	lda 2,s	;A = srcdst banks	cpx #$FFFF	;Was there a bank cross?	bne muXNot0	;C = 1 if =	sbc #$0100	;Dec 1 from source bank better not wrap!muXNot0	cpy #$FFFF	;Did destination cross bank?	bne muYIs0	dec AmuYIs0	sta 2,s	ENTRY muFirstmuFirst		; 	cpx TempCount	;Will Source cross bank?	bcs muXOk	;Br if no cross	stx TempCount	;Only move X bytesmuXOk	cpy TempCount	;Will destination cross bank?	bcs muYOk	sty TempCountmuYOk	lda #(muReturn-1)>>8	pha	;Push return address	lda #(MuReturn-1)<<8 ;Low byte of ret addr and bank 0	pha	tsc	clc	;Addr of code	adc #4	pha	lda TempCount	;Get # bytes to move	rtl	;Takes us to the move codemuReturn	lda Count	;Count = Count - Bytes moved	clc	;Actual bytes moved	1 more than count	sbc TempCount	sta Count	sta TempCount	lda Count+2	;Now do high word	sbc #0	bpl muMore	;Br if more to do	pla	;Pull move code off	of stack	pla	pea $E1E1	;Fix data bank	plb	plb	rtl********************************************************************************** MoveDown* This is used if Source >= Destination* inputs: X = >Source*********************************************************************************	ENTRY MoveDownMoveDown		; 	ldy Dest* First put move code in mem: MVN dst src RTL	lda Source+2	;Get source bank	and #$00FF	;Ignore high byte	ora #$6B00	;RTL Opcode	pha	lda Dest+2	;Destination Bank	xba	ora #$54	;MVN opcode	pha	lda Count	;Init TempCount	sta TempCount	bra mdFirstMdMore	sta Count+2	;More bytes to move	lda 2,s	;A = SrcDest banks	cpx #1	;Bank Cross?  if X=0	bcs mdXNot0	adc #$0100	;Add 1 to source bankmdXNot0	cpy #0	;Did destination cross bank?	bne mdYIs0	inc AmdYIs0	sta 2,s	ENTRY mdFirstmdFirst		; 	txa	;If Count > -X then	bank cross	eor #$FFFF	cmp TempCount	bcs MdXOk	sta TempCount	;Only move -X bytesmdXOk	tya	;Will destination cross bank?	eor #$FFFF	cmp TempCount	bcs mdYOk	sta TempCount	;Only move -Y bytesmdYOk	lda #(mdReturn-1)>>8	pha	;Push return address	lda #(MdReturn-1)<<8 ;Low byte of ret addr and bank 0	pha	tsc	clc	;Addr of code	adc #4	pha	lda TempCount	;Get # bytes to move	rtl	;Takes us to the move codemdReturn	lda Count	;Count = Count - Bytes moved	clc	;Actual bytes moved	1 more than count	sbc TempCount	sta Count	sta TempCount	lda Count+2	;Now do high word	sbc #0	bpl mdMore	;Br if more to do	pla	;Pop move code off of stack	pla	pea $E1E1	plb	plb	rtl	ENDP	Title ' Compaction Routines'********************************************************************************** SearchFail - Called when unable to find a segment*              This	routine decides what sort of compaction, etc. to do*              If in an interrupt, no compaction or purging	is done.**  So what does it do?**  First, we looke at the IRQActive flag.  If we are inside an interrupt,*  we must not move or dispose of anything.  We can only fail.**  If we can try and make room we look at the retry count:**     1:  Let User try*     2:  Compact*     3:  Purge Level 3's*     4:  Purge Level 2's*     5:  Purge Level 1's*     6:  Let user try one last time.**** Output:      C = 1 if ok to retry** Change History** 1 Dec 88	Steven Glass** Added call to clear recent in Level1 checking.  This prevents* handles that are purged from being left in the recent list.**********************************************************************************XSearchFail	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	import ClearRecent;-----------------------------------------------------------;; First, see if we can even try to do anything.;	clc	lda |IrqActive	;In an interrupt?	and #$00FF	bne GiveUp	inc Retry	; bump the retry count and see how many times	lda Retry	; we've been here	cmp #7;;;	bcs GiveUp	bcs myGiveUp	;19-Dec-91 DAL	asl a	tax	jmp (FailTable,x)FailTable	dc.w 0	dc.w FirstTry	dc.w SecondTry	dc.w ThirdTry	dc.w FourthTry	dc.w FifthTry	dc.w SixthTry*** added 19-Dec-91 DALmyGiveUp	clc	rtl*** end 19-Dec-91;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Let the user try first.;FirstTry	jsr ClearRecent    IF RAMVersion THEN	jsl xUserPurge    ELSE	jsl UserPurge    ENDIF		bcc UserCouldNotHelp	rtlUserCouldNotHelp	inc Retry	;Bump the retry count	lda Retry	; and fall into second try;-----------------------------------------------------------;; This is the second time in, so we just compact and ; try again.;SecondTry	jsl Compact	sec	rtl;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Third, fourth and fifth try:  We purge the level 3's, ; 2's and 1's.;ThirdTryFourthTryFifthTry	jsl Purge	;Try purging	bcs SecondTry	;It may have worked, compact the result; Fall into Sixth Try;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Egads, this is our last chance.  Call the user and ; beg him to do something.;SixthTry    IF RAMVersion THEN	jsl xUserPurge    ELSE	jsl UserPurge    ENDIF	bcc GiveUp;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Wow, the user thinks he can help us out.  So we go through and ; purge everything that can be purged.  Compact memory one last time; and try again.;	PushWord #0	_PurgeAll	bra SecondTry; User could not do anything.  We must give up.  Return with the carry clear.GiveUp	rtl	ENDP	eject********************************************************************************** Compact -    This	routine attempts to	move all memory blocks upwards*              Blocks that are fixed or	locked are not moved** Revision 2:  If compaction for fixed block in banks 0 or 1,*               only compact 0 and 1*********************************************************************************XCompact	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr BestTop	;Get top to start from. Rev 2* First move zero page down for a new temporary ZP.  Don't change X	phd	;Save current ZP	tsc	sec	sbc #ZPSize	tcs	tcd* Starting from the	top of memory, go through all of the segments	jsr StartXTop	;X from best top* to move to the next block, set the following* Hndl1      -> Hndl2* Hndl2.Prev -> Hndl1 if nil then done* Hndl1.Size -> Size* Hndl1.Owner-> Owner actually not needed but moved in loop* Hndl1.Attr -> Attr* Hndl1.Addr -> Addr, Addr1* Hndl2.Addr -> Addr2	ENTRY NextBlockNextBlock		; 	move_l Hndl1,Hndl2	;Hndl1 -> Hndl2	ldy #hndl_prev+2	;Hndl2.Prev -> Hndl1	lda [Hndl2],y	sta Hndl1+2	dey	dey	lda [Hndl2],y	sta Hndl1	ora Hndl1+2	;If Nil then done	beq Done	dey	;Move rest of Hndl1	data	deyMvLoop1	lda [Hndl1],y	tyx	sta Addr,x	dey	dey	cpy #hndl_attr	;Move down through attr	bge MvLoop1	;Exit loop with attr in A	bit #attr_locked+attr_fixed	bne NextBlock	;Skip the block if it can't moveMvLoop2	tyx	lda [Hndl1],y	;Now Move the addresses	sta addr,x	sta addr1,x	lda [Hndl2],y	sta addr2,x	dey	dey	bpl MvLoop2* Now check if the block can move	jsr CheckFit	lda addr1	;If addr <> addr1 then move it	cmp addr	bne ItMoved	lda addr1+2	cmp addr+2	beq NextBlock	;No move, Go do the	next Block* Slide the block up Source = Addr, Count = Size (equivalent equates)ItMoved		; 	lda addr1	;Store new address in handle	sta [Hndl1]	sta Dest	;Also set destination	ldy #hndl_addr+2	lda addr1+2	sta [Hndl1],y	sta Dest+2	jsl MoveData	;Do the move. Hndl1	unchanged!!!!	bra NextBlockDone		; 	tsc	;Pull the stack back up	clc	adc #ZPSize	tcs	pld	;And fix zero page	rtl	ENDP********************************************************************************** UserPurge - allows user to mark blocks purgeable** This routine calls each of the installed OOM routines with telling them* how much memory is needed.** If enough total memory is freed, this routine returns carry set, * otherwise it returns carry clear.** Inputs:*          Size Of block needed** Outputs:     *          C = 1 if OK to repurge and compact*          C = 0 if its not worth trying again*** Change History** 10 Sep 88	Steven Glass** This routine had always existed, but had never done anything until today.** 02 Oct 88	Steven Glass** This routine is now called before and after compact and purging.  The* retry value is used to determine which it is.  When we are called first* we only call user routines that have bit 0 set in the TaskFlags.** When we are called second, we only call user routines that have bit 1* set in the task flags.** 16 Oct 88	Steven Glass** We now call all routines all the time but we pass a retry count.  0 if* this is before the memory manager has done anything.  1 if its later.*********************************************************************************XUserPurge	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on	DSect 0TaskLink	LONGTaskFlags	WORDTaskSignature	WORDTaskEntry	LONG	DefineStackOrigDirect	wordRetryValue	wordSizeNeeded	LONGCurPtr	LONGAmountFreed	LONG	lda |FirstOOMPtr+2	; is there any?	tax	; copy in x for below	ora |FirstOOMPtr	bne GoAndTry	clc	rtlGoAndTry	pha	; push space for the space freed	pha	phx	; push the pointer to the first header	lda |FirstOOMPtr	pha	pei Size+2	; push the size needed	pei Size	pei Retry	phd	; push d-page	tsc	; turn stack to d-page	tcd	stz AmountFreed	; zero the amount we freed	stz AmountFreed+2;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Reset Retry value to 1 or 2 depending or its original; value.  This way we can use the RetryValue as a mask; to decide which routines to run.;	ldx #$0000	lda RetryValue	cmp #1	beq @1	ldx #1@1	stx RetryValueNextOne			pha	pha	pei SizeNeeded+2	pei SizeNeeded	pei RetryValue	jsl CallThisOne	pla	clc	adc AmountFreed	sta AmountFreed	pla	adc AmountFreed+2	sta AmountFreed+2;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Point to next one.;SkipThisOne	lda [CurPtr]	tax	ldy #2	lda [CurPtr],y	sta CurPtr+2	stx CurPtr	ora CurPtr	bne NextOne;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Was enough freed?;;; 3/31/89	Mensch; Correct the following compare...; was:;	lda SizeNeeded;	sec;	sbc AmountFreed;	lda SizeNeeded+2;	sbc AmountFreed+2;	bcc Enough;	beq Enough;; Compare sizeNeeded to amount freed as follows...;  If SizeNeeded+2 < AmountFreed+2 then enough;;  If SizeNeeded+2 = AmountFreed+2 then ;    If AmountFreed >= SizeNeeded then enough;      else @TooSmall;;    else @TooSmall;;	lda SizeNeeded+2	; first test to see if we freed way to much	cmp AmountFreed+2	; by comparing the high words...	blt Enough	; if its less than amount freed, we have more than enough memory	bne @TooSmall	; if on the other hand, size needed is not; SizeNeeded+2 = AmountNeeded+2 here	lda AmountFreed		cmp SizeNeeded	bge Enough	; if Amount>=SizeNeeded then we got enough@TooSmall	clc	bra FixStackEnough	sec;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Fix the stack and get out.;FixStack	pld	; pull d-page	pla	; pull retry value	pla	; pull Size	pla	pla	; pull OOM Pointer	pla	pla	; pull Amount freed	pla	rtl	; all done;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Little routine to check the signature and ; call the routine.;CallThisOne	ldy #TaskSignature	lda [CurPtr],y	cmp #QueueSignature	bne Die	lda CurPtr	clc	adc #TaskEntry	pei CurPtr+1	phb	dec a	sta 1,s	rtlDie	PushWord #OOMQueueDamaged	PushLong #0	_SysFailMgr	ENDP*****************************************************************AddToOOMQueue	PROC EXPORT** Adds the specified routine to the list of routines that are* run when the memory manager runs out of memory.** Possible Errors:** InvalidHeader*** Inputs:*	PointerToHeader** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************    IF RAMVersion THEN	jsl xlink    ELSE	jsl link    ENDIF		pei Parms+2	pei Parms	pea FirstOOMPtr>>16	pea |FirstOOMPtr	_AddToQueue	sta error	; pass on error code if any to the cleanup routines 	    IF RAMVersion THEN	jml xCleanUp    ELSE	jml CleanUp    ENDIF	ENDP*****************************************************************DeleteFromOOMQueue	PROC EXPORT** Removes the specified routine to the list of routines that are* run when the memory manager runs out of memory.** Possible Errors:** InvalidHeader* NotInQueue** Inputs:*	PointerToHeader** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	    IF RAMVersion THEN	jsl xlink    ELSE	jsl link    ENDIF			pei Parms+2	pei Parms	pea FirstOOMPtr>>16	pea |FirstOOMPtr	_DeleteFromQueue	sta error	; pass on error code if any to the cleanup routines 	    IF RAMVersion THEN	jml xCleanUp    ELSE	jml CleanUp    ENDIF		ENDP	title ' Purge Routines'********************************************************************************** XPurge - purges blocks from memory until size bytes have been freed**           Yea from the table of my memory*           I'll sweep away all trivial	fond records*	    Shakespeare, Hamlet, I. v. 96** Inputs:      Size	= block we are trying to allocate*              Retry =  retry count*	    2 = purge level	3 (zombies)*	    3 = purge level	2*	    4 = purge level	1*	   >4 = nothing left to purge** Outputs:     C = 1 if OK to retry*              Retry = next retry count	- 1 (its inced before we're called)** ZP used:     hndl1, hndl2, addr1, addr2 rest unchanged** Revision 2:  Now in the rom*              If Purging for fixed address in banks 0 or 1*               routine only purges out	of 0 and 1*** Change History** 16 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Changed in line constants to equates for LastRetry and ZombieRetry.* These had to change when I changed the SearchFail routine to call the* user before doing other things.  This meant that retry was much high* when this routine was called.*********************************************************************************XPurge	PROC EXPORT	longa on	longi on* Local equatesPHndl	equ addr1	;Handle being checked to purgePSize	equ addr2	;# bytes to purgeLastRetry	equ 6ZombieRetry	equ 3* If retry > LastRetry then we can't purge any more	lda Retry	cmp #LastRetry	;A has retry count	bcc RetryOK	clc	rtlRetryOK	ldx size	;Get the size to purge	stx PSize	ldx size+2	stx PSize+2** To start, hndl2 =	top block which isn't purgeable*           phndl =	next down which might be*	ENTRY StartTopStartTop		; 	rep #$10	;StartTop needs 16 bit X	jsr BestTop	;Find the best top to start from	sep #$10	;ldy # faster than dey dey	longi off	lda |MemList,x	;Only need the low 8 bits from besttop	sta phndl	lda |MemList+2,x	sta phndl+2	ldy #hndl_prev+2	;Get next down	lda [phndl],y	sta hndl1+2	ldy #hndl_prev	lda [phndl],y	sta hndl1PurgeLoop	jsr NextPurge	;Get next purgable block	bcc EndOfList	jsr NukeIt	;Purge the block	lda retry	;Killing zombies	cmp #ZombieRetry	beq KillZombies	;If killing zombies, then get the rest	lda hndl2	;hndl2 -> phndl to make NextPurge work	sta phndl	lda hndl2+2	sta phndl+2	lda psize+2	;Need to purge any more?	bpl PurgeLoop	bra Done** Here we purge the	rest of the zombies	of the same owner*KillZombies	ldy #hndl_owner	;Get the owner	lda [phndl],y	and #$F0FF	;Mask off aux id	pha	ENTRY ZombieLoopZombieLoop		; 	lda hndl2	;hndl2 -> phndl to make NextPurge work	sta phndl	lda hndl2+2	sta phndl+2ZombieSkip	jsr NextPurge	bcc LastZombie	ldy #hndl_owner	;Get owner	lda [phndl],y	and #$F0FF	cmp 1,s	;Is it the one we want?	bne ZombieSkip	;Skip it if not	jsr NukeIt	;Purge it	bra ZombieLoopLastZombie	pla	;All of owner purged. fix the stack	lda psize	;Purged enough?	bpl StartTop	;Start again if not* Hooray, we urged enoughDone		; 	dec Retry	;It will be inced before we are called	rep #$10	sec	rtl	ENTRY EndOfListEndOfList		; 	inc Retry	;Go to next level	lda Retry	cmp #LastRetry	bcc StartTop	;if <= LastRetry then start another pass	bra Done	;Other wise try what we have********************************************************************************** NextPurge - Finds	next purgable block** To get to the next:   phndl -> hndl2*	    hndl1 -> hndl*	    phndl.prev -> hndl1 if nil then done** outputs: C = 0 then end of list*********************************************************************************	ENTRY NextPurgeNextPurge		; 	longa on	longi off	ldx Retry	;Make mask for purging	lda >Purgemask-ZombieRetry-1,x	and #$FF00	pha	;Save it on the stack	ENTRY LoopLoop		; 	move_l phndl,hndl2	move_l hndl1,phndl	ldy #hndl_prev+2	lda [phndl],y	sta hndl1+2	ldy #hndl_prev	lda [phndl],y	sta hndl1	ora hndl1+2	;= nil?	beq IsNil	;Br if so	lda attr	;If No spec allowed	bit #attr_nospec	beq CheckIt	ldy #hndl_addr+2	;Then stop if in bank1	lda [phndl],y	lsr A	;= 0 if bank 0 or 1	beq IsNil* Now check if we can purge itCheckIt	ldy #hndl_attr	;Get the attributes	lda [phndl],y	bmi Loop	;Skip if locked	and #attr_purge	;Purgable?	cmp 1,s	bcc Loop	;Br if < level we are looking for	sec	;Found one	pla	rtsIsNil	clc	pla	rts	ENTRY PurgeMaskPurgeMask	DC.B 3,2,1********************************************************************************** NukeIt - Purges the block* Here we purge the	block. Since it is purgable, hndl1 & hndl2 aren't nil* To purge hndl:	    hndl2 -> hndl1.next*	    hndl1 -> hndl2.prev    This removes	hndl from the list*	    PurgeList -> phndl.next*	    nil   -> phndl.prev*	    phndl -> PurgeList.prev*	    phndl -> PurgeList*	    nil   -> phndl.addr    This purges hndl**	    psize - phndl.size -> psize** notes: A pointer to the current head of purgelist is put on the stack*********************************************************************************	ENTRY NukeItNukeIt		; 	longa on	longi off	phb	ldy #hndl_next	lda hndl2	sta [hndl1],y	lda |PurgeList	pha	;Save for stack based pointer	sta [phndl],y	;Attach rest of purge list to phndl	ldy #hndl_next+2	;Remove it from used list	lda hndl2+2	;hndl2 -> hndl1.next	sta [hndl1],y	lda |PurgeList+2	;Attach rest of purge list to phndl	sta [phndl],y	tay	;Y = bank of head of purgelist	phy	ldy #hndl_prev+2	;hndl1 -> hndl2.prev	lda hndl1+2	sta [hndl2],y	ldy #hndl_prev	lda hndl1	sta [hndl2],y	lda #0	;nil -> phndl.prev	sta [phndl],y	ldy #hndl_prev+2	sta [phndl],y	ldy #hndl_addr+2	;nil -> hndl.addr	sta [phndl],y	sta [phndl]	lda phndl+2	;hndl -> PurgeList	sta |PurgeList+2	lda phndl	sta |PurgeList	plb	;phndl -> OldPurgeList.prev	ldy #hndl_prev	sta (1,s),y	lda phndl+2	ldy #hndl_prev+2	sta (1,s),y	pla	;Fix stack	plb	;and bank* Now subtract amount+1 purged from total needed	ldy #hndl_size	lda psize	clc	;Extra -1 so just the right size will	sbc [phndl],y	;go minus instead of 0	sta psize	ldy #hndl_size+2	lda psize+2	sbc [phndl],y	sta psize+2	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************CheckRecent	PROC EXPORT** Checks the handle in hndl and sees if it is one of the* last allocated handles that we keep to speed up searching** If it is we replace the lastfound handle with its prior or* next handle.*** Inputs:*	hndl*	LastLowHandle*	LastHighHandle** Outputs:*	LastLowHandle*	LastHighHandle** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 06 Nov 88	Steven Glass** To try and improve our shortcut hit rate, i've changed* what we do when the handle being removed is the recent* handle.  I make the recent handle equal to the prior or* next handle.** 30 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Must make sure that the handle we are looking for is * real.  Had problem when zero was passed to dispose and * the recent handle value was 0.** 14-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Steve!  LastLowHandle and LastHighHandle can be equal!* Removed the branch to handle this caes correctly.*****************************************************************	lda hndl+2	beq @Continue	cmp |LastLowHandle+2	bne @NotLow	lda hndl	cmp |LastLowHandle	bne @NotLow	ldy #Hndl_Prev	; since this one is going away, get replace it with prior	lda [hndl],y	sta |LastLowHandle	ldy #Hndl_Prev+2	lda [hndl],y	sta |LastLowHandle+2****** Removed this BRA 14-Sep-91 DAL.  Memory Manager was exploding if the*** high and low hints "crossed," then became equal, and then somebody*** disposed of the handle that both hints were pointing at.  Only the*** low one was getting bumped, leaving us with a high hint that was*** actually the first handle on the free list (so the backwards link is*** nil)!  If the very next NewHandle was for non-fixed memory, it would*** get Very Confused when finding a nil backwards link on what should be*** a valid used handle.***;;;	bra @Continue***@NotLow	lda hndl	cmp |LastHighHandle	bne @Continue	lda hndl+2	cmp |LastHighHandle+2	bne @Continue	ldy #Hndl_Next	; since this one is going away, get replace it with next	lda [hndl],y	sta |LastHighHandle	ldy #Hndl_Next+2	lda [hndl],y	sta |LastHighHandle+2@continue;-----------------------------------------------------------	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************ClearRecent	PROC** Zeros the values in LastLowHandle and LastHighHandle** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda #0	sta >LastLowHandle	sta >LastLowHandle+2	sta >LastHighHandle	sta >LastHighHandle+2	rts	ENDP	title ' RamDisk Command routines'********************************************************************************** GetDiskSize - Returns the current size of the RamDisk*********************************************************************************GetDiskSize	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >CurDiskSize	sta 7,s	lda >curDiskSize+2	sta 9,s	jmp QuickExit	ENDP	title 'Routines	for making the disk'	eject********************************************************************************** MakeDisk - Creates a single handle for the ramdisk memory** Outputs:     C=1 if failed  C=0 if Succeeded*********************************************************************************MakeDisk	PROC	longa on	longi on	stz |CurDiskSize	;Zero things out	stz |CurDiskSize+2	stz |DiskHandles	stz |DiskHandles+2	stz |FormatFlag	;Mark Unformatted* First get the TotalMem size	pushlong #0000	_TotalMem	pla 	pla	;a = 64K banks of RAM* Get maximum size.	 If > available then use the max available	longa off	longi off	sep #$30	dec A	;-2 since 0 & 1 not	used for ram disk	dec A	asl A	;A = # 32K chunks available	cmp |MaxDiskParm	;Is it less than requested?	blt TooBig	;Br if requested size is too big	lda |MaxDiskParm	;Use the requested sizeTooBig	tax	;This clears the high byte	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	txa	;a = # of 32K units in RamDisk	beq NoDisk	;RD size is zero so exit	pha	;save for later	pushlong #0000	;space for newhandle result	lsr A	;convert to units of 64K	pha	;push hi word of length	sta |CurDiskSize+2	lda #0000	ror A	;put 32K bit in msb	pha	;push lo word of length	sta |CurDiskSize*  create the handle needed for the RAMdisk	pushword #RDiskID	;Owner ID for the ramdisk	pushword #Attr_NoSpec+Attr_Page  ;attributes for RAMdisk memory	pushlong #0000	;any address please	_NewHandle		pla	sta hndl	pla	sta hndl+2	bcs NoDisk2	;clear stack before BCS  01/19/89 JOA	sta |DiskHandles+2	lda hndl	sta |DiskHandles	;Save the handle of the block* deref the handle in hndl into the pointer addr	geth_l hndl,addr,hndl_addr* Now set the block	size	pla	;get back # of 32K units	tax	;save for zap	asl A	asl A	asl A	asl A	asl A	asl A	;A = # 512 byte blocks	sta |BlockSize	;BlockSize = maxblock # +1* Now I have to zero out the entire block!zapnxt	lda #0000	tay@zlp	sta [addr],y	iny	iny	bpl @zlp	tya	clc	adc addr 	sta addr	bcc @10	inc addr+2@10	dex	;another 32K hunk to zap?	bne zapnxtDone	clc	rtsNoDisk2	pla	;Fix the stack	stz |CurDiskSize	;and clear the RD size	stz |CurDiskSize+2	; so nobody thinks anything hereNoDisk	sec	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** GetDiskBlock - Gets a block of the ram disk** Inputs:      PCBlockNum = Block number** Outputs:     hndl	= handle containing	disk*              addr	= starting address of block in handle*              C = 1 if unable to get block** GetBlockA - Block	number is in the A reg********************************************************************************GetDiskBlock	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >PCBlockNum+2	;High word must be 0	bne BadBlock	lda >PCBlockNum	ENTRY GetBlockAGetBlockA		;       	cmp |BlockSize	bge BadBlock* Get the 1 handle and add blocknum*512 to addressBlockOK	pha	;Save blocknumber for later	lda |DiskHandles	;Get the handle we want	sta hndl	lda |DiskHandles+2	;Carry	sta hndl+2	;hndl is handle containing block	beq NoBlock	;Br if no ramdisk!!!!!	geth_l hndl,addr,hndl_addr ;Get the address* now add blocknum*512 to the addr 	pla	;Get the block number again	asl A	;Leaves C = 0 and A = block# * 2	adc addr+1	;add at + 1 for block# * 256	sta addr+1	;Thus addr = addr+(Blknum*512)	clc	rtsBadBlock	lda #PCBadBlk	bra NoBlock2NoBlock	lda #PCIOErr	;ioerror	pla	;Fix the stackNoBlock2	sta error	sec	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** RDFormat - Makes a catalog in the ramdisk if needed** inputs: A = Protocol converter command*********************************************************************************RDFormat	PROC	longa on	longi on	cmp #$0005	;Don't format if PCinit	beq NoFormat	bit |FormatFlag	;Already formatted?	bmi NoFormat* Get the block and	put a catalog in it	pha	;Save command #	lda #$0000	;Index from block 0	jsr GetBlockA	bcs NoBlock	;Br if can't get block	lda >ProFlag	;0 if pascal <>0 if	ProDOS	ldx #PasCat-ProCat	;Assume Pascal	ldy #$040E	;Y = where size goes	and #$00FF	beq IsPascal* It's a prodos catalog* First make the bit map	lda |BlockSize	lsr A	;Get # words in bitmap	lsr A	lsr A	lsr A	tay	;Y = # words	xba	;Get # blocks in bitmap	asl A	and #$000F	tax	lda >BitMap,x	;First word has directory busy	tyx	ldy #$0C00	;Block 6 = bitmapBitLoop	sta [addr],y	iny	iny	lda #$FFFF	;Rest are FFs	dex	bne BitLoop	ldx #0	;X = index into catalog table	ldy #$0429	;Store number of blocksIsPascal	lda |BlockSize	;Move the block size	sta [addr],y** This part moves the catalog*CatLoop	lda >ProCat,x	inx	inx	cmp #Flag	;Address flag?	bne NoFlag	lda >ProCat,x	;Get new address	beq NoMore	;Br if end of table	inx	inx	tay	bra CatLoopNoFlag	sta [addr],y	iny	iny	bra CatLoopNoMore	lda #True	sta |FormatFlag	;Mark FormattedNoBlock	pla	;Get command # backNoFormat	rts* Catalog imageFlag	equ $FEFE	;Flag to mark address change* This is the prodos catalog image Must	be an even number of bytesProCat		; 	DC.W Flag	;Block 2	DC.B $02,$04,$03,$00	DC.B $F4	DC.B 'RAM5'	DC.B $00	DC.W Flag	DC.B $22,$04,$C3,$27,$0D,$00,$00,$06	DC.W Flag	;Block 3	DC.B $00,$06,$02,$00,$04,$00	DC.W Flag	;Block 4	DC.B $00,$08,$03,$00,$05,$00	DC.W Flag	DC.B $00,$0A,$04,$00	DC.W Flag,	0* Table of first word bitmapsBitMap		; 	DC.B $01,$FF	;Up to 2M	DC.B $00,$FF	;4M	DC.B $00,$7F	;6M	DC.B $00,$3F	;8M	DC.B $00,$1F	;10M	DC.B $00,$0F	;12M	DC.B $00,$07	;14M	DC.B $00,$03	;16MPasCat		; 	DC.W Flag	;Block 2 byte 2	DC.B $02,$04	DC.B $06,$00,$00,$00,$04	DC.B 'RAM5'	DC.B $00	DC.W Flag,	0	ENDP	title ' RamDisk Protocol Converter Command'********************************************************************************** ExecPCCmd - Executes a protocol converter command** Extend calls are mapped into normal calls for dispatch* The command table	is in real page 0** Rev 2 change: returns 1 byte error code.  Word move was trashing byte count**********************************************************************************ExecPCCmd	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsl RDLink	lda >PCCommand	;Get the command	and #$00FF	;Only low word valid	cmp #0010	;0 - 9 are normal calls	bcc CmdOK	and #%10111111	;40 - 49 -> 0 - 9	cmp #0010	bcc CmdOk	jsr NotImp	bra CmdbadxitCmdOK	jsr RDFormat	;Format the ramdisk	if needed	asl A	;*2 for table look up	tax	jsr (PCDispatch,x)	;Go do the commandCmdbadxit	sep #$20	;8 bit error code Rev 2 change	lda error	;Get Error code	sta >PCStatByte	;To return the error	rep #$20	;back to 16 bits	jmp XCleanUp	;All done	ENTRY PCDispatchPCDispatch		; 	DC.W PCStatus	;0, $40 Status command	DC.W PCReadBlk	;1, $41 Read Block	DC.W PCWriteBlk	;2, $42 Write Block	DC.W Null	;3, $43 Format	DC.W PCControl	;4, $44 Control	DC.W PCInit	;5, $45 Init	DC.W NotImp	;6, $46 Open	DC.W NotImp	;7, $47 Close	DC.W NotImp	;8, $48 Read	DC.W NotImp	;9, $49 WriteNotImp	lda #PCBadCmd	;Bad command	sta errorNull	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PCStatus - protocol converter status call** Only calls 0 & 3 are valid*********************************************************************************PCStatus	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >PCStatCode	;Get status code	and #$00FF	;Only want low byte	beq StatusOK	;Br if status 0	cmp #$0003	;DIB call?	beq StatusOK	lda #PCBadCtl	;Return Bad Status Error	sta Error	rts	ENTRY StatusOKStatusOK		; 	pha	;Save Code for later	lda >PCBuffer	;Get the buffer	sta dest	lda >PCBuffer+2	and #$00FF	sta dest+2	ldy #2	;If normal command 0 out 3rd and 4th	lda >PCCommand	;Was it an extended	command?	and #$0040	beq NormCmd	iny	;Else do the 4th and 5thNormCmd	lda #0	sta [dest],y	iny	iny	;Y = Bytes transferred (4 or 5)	lda >BlockSize	;Get #Blocks	tax	;Save for later	beq Is0	;OffLine if Size 0	lda #$00F8	;Mark OnLineIs0	ora #$00E8	;If A was 0 then offline	sta [dest]	;Give user the status	txa	tyx	;Now X has bytes transferred	ldy #1	sta [dest],y	txy	;Y has transferred again	pla	;Do we want the DIB	too?	beq StatDone	;All done if call 0* Now transferr the	DIB too	sep #$30	;Easier Since it an	odd length table	longa off	longi off	ldx #0	;Index into DIBDIBLoop	lda >DIB,x	sta [dest],y	iny	inx	cpx #DIBLen	blt DibLoop	rep #$30	longa on	longi onStatDone	tya	;Get # bytes transferred	sta >PCXferCount	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PCReadBlk - Read a block from the ram	disk** PCMove - entry point from PCWriteBlk to move 512 bytes of	data*********************************************************************************PCReadBlk	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr GetDiskBlock	;Get the block	bcs BadBlock	;Br if bad; Set up parameters	to read block Source already set up in Addr	lda >PCBuffer	;Get destination	sta dest	lda >PCBuffer+2	and #$00FF	sta dest+2	ENTRY PCMovePCMove		;       	stz count+2	;Move 512 bytes	lda #512	sta count	sta >PCXferCount	jsl MoveDataBadBlock	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PCWriteBlk - Writes a block to the ram disk*********************************************************************************PCWriteBlk	PROC	longa on	longi on	jsr GetDiskBlock	;Get the block	bcs BadBlock	;Br if bad	move_l addr,dest	;Get the data	lda >PCBuffer	;Get source	sta source	lda >PCBuffer+2	and #$00FF	sta source+2	bra PCMove	;Go move the dataBadBlock	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PCControl - protocol converter control call** Only call 0 (reset device)  is  valid*********************************************************************************PCControl	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda >PCStatCode	;Get control code	and #$00FF	;Only want low byte	beq ControlOK	;Br if reset	lda #PCBadCtl	;Return Bad Status Error	sta ErrorControlOK	rts	ENDP********************************************************************************** PCInit -     Initialization call from	the protocol converter*********************************************************************************PCInit	PROC	longa on	longi on	lda #0	sta >PCXferCount	lda |BlockSize	bne DiskOK	;Br if there is already a disk	jsr MakeDisk	bcc DiskOK	lda #PCNoDrive	;No drive error	sta errorDiskOK	rts	ENDP	Title 'Equates for the protocol converter'********************************************************************************** Equates for the protocol converter*********************************************************************************PCData	PROC* The Device information block	ENTRY DIBDIB		; 	DC.B 7	;Name length	;     1234567890123456	DC.B 'RAMCARD         '	DC.B $00	;Type	DC.B $C0	;Extended and disk switched	DC.B $00,$10	;Version	ENDP	END